; nova-tools roadmap: work planned for the release after the current one.
; Moved out of the nova-sprint sprint (epoch 15) on 2026-10-04 by the coordinator, on Glenn Fiedler's word:
; "for the later release work, I'd like you to remove this from this sprint, making sure it is stored
;  somewhere in a sexp data structure". Each card keeps its whole brief, so it can be added back as it is:
;  nova-sprint add --stream <stream> --brief-file <the card's :brief written to <id>.md>.
; ROADMAP.md is generated from this file.
(:roadmap 1 :repo "mas-bandwidth/nova-tools" :product "nova-tools" :generated "2026-10-04"
 :source "nova-sprint store, epoch 15, cards waiting when the release was cut"
 :releases
 ((:release "v1.3.0" :status :planned :cards 507
   :streams
   ((:stream "rerate-v1-2-0" :cards
     ((:id "rerate-alex-swarm" :tier "-" :needs ("after-nova-tools-v1-2-0") :who "friend.alex"
      :title "Rate nova-swarm as released in nova-tools v1.2.0: read its help (`nova-swarm help` and every verb's -h) and its spec cold, then use it for real on a throwaway store or directory (never a live store, never a server started on this machine), "
      :brief "REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: fix-red
CLASS: model
WHO: friend alex
LEG: go
DEADLINE: finish within 90 minutes
DEPENDS-ON: after-nova-tools-v1-2-0
PATHS: docs/ratings/1.2.0/nova-swarm-alex.md
NEW: docs/ratings/1.2.0/nova-swarm-alex.md
TEST: ./internal/ci TestRatingFileIsInForm
Deadline: finish within 90 minutes.
Libraries considered: none; a rating card: the tool as released, read cold and used for real on a throwaway store or directory. (Glenn, 2026-10-04 12:58 PM: once nova-tools v1.2.0 lands, a re-review from friends around each tool, now that it is reduced to the set that is in there.)

ATTRIBUTION: commits and reports name the friend (By: Alex) and your actual model and harness. Never claim a model or harness you are not running. A Claude worker writes the true Claude trailer.

You are a friend of the coordinator, and this card is one sprint job (docs/FRIENDS.md), delivered as `~/alex-working/inbox/<job>/BRIEF.md`: its STATUS line names the epoch, attempt and branch to push. Work only under `~/alex-working/jobs/<job>/`, using `~/alex-working/.cache/go-build`. In this card, JOB.md means the delivered BRIEF.md.

THE TASK. Rate nova-swarm as released in nova-tools v1.2.0: read its help (`nova-swarm help` and every verb's -h) and its spec cold, then use it for real on a throwaway store or directory (never a live store, never a server started on this machine), and rate READ x/10 and USE x/10 for the question \"Is this a good tool for an AI to use?\" (the goal is 10/10). List every defect as one TSV line in the report: tool, verb or file:line, defect, the fix. The rating file is docs/ratings/1.2.0/nova-swarm-alex.md in the FORM of docs/ratings/1.1.0 (title, Build: the head's sha, 12 hex, Reasons, Findings, Good keep, Compared with earlier ratings).

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/alex-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of origin/dev. Export GOCACHE=~/alex-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Build the tool: `go build -o $JOB/bin/nova-swarm ./cmd/nova-swarm`.

STEP 2. Read cold, use for real on a throwaway, rate, and write the rating file; every defect one TSV line in the PR body and the outbox report.
  PATHS: docs/ratings/1.2.0/nova-swarm-alex.md
  COMMIT: rerate-alex-swarm: READ and USE rating of nova-swarm for v1.2.0.
  VERDICT: the rating file is in FORM with both scores and reasons; every defect is a TSV line; nothing but the one file changed.

STEP 3. Obtain the shared Go-slot grant, then run `nice -n 19 env GOMAXPROCS=2 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci -run 'TestRatingFileIsInForm|TestGeneralityText'`, record exact last lines, release the slot, and commit only PATHS with honest Alex and actual model/harness attribution.

STEP 4. END. Push normally with `git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/<the STATUS line's branch>`; never force. Verify `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<that branch>` equals `git rev-parse HEAD`. Write `~/alex-working/outbox/<job>/REPORT.md` beginning `Verdict: LAND` and `Head: <full 40-hex remote tip>`, followed by one paragraph stating the change and exact gates. Use HOLD or FAIL with the precise blocker when no truthful LAND is possible. Write RESULT.md beside it carrying this card's RESULT line. Create no pull request; the sprint consumes the branch and report.

DONE-WHEN: the rating file is committed in FORM and the defect TSV is in the report.

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.")
