THE TASK. A tree of 1 work step (STEP 2 to STEP 2), walked in order. Each work step carries its own PATHS:, COMMIT: and VERDICT: lines: do it, run its check, commit only its PATHS with its COMMIT: line as the message, and write its verdict line in the PR body and RESULT, `step <n>: <ok|broken|not-done|skipped> <the full 40-hex commit sha pasted from git rev-parse HEAD, or - when nothing changed; a short sha is refused: e.g. step 2: ok 3b1f0c2a9d4e7f6a5c8b1d0e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f90 the change> <one line>` (ok with `-` and the commit that did it when the head already holds the step). The first step that is not ok stops the walk: steps before it land, and the coordinator turns the rest into a new card. Compact the tests (the owner: \"mechanical conversion first, then we try to compact the tests using whatever means are necessary\"; \"If you have written fully perfect, optimal minimal representation of tests already, I'll be SHOCKED\"). Use the package's rig (the `rig_test.go` its harness card wrote: read it, never edit it) and internal/testkit; turn tests that differ only by data into one table with named rows under `t.Run`; let a helper own a repeated failure sentence; turn repeated setup into a rig call; delete comments that restate the code. Every pinned behaviour stays pinned (count the checks before and after; break three behaviours in the code on purpose, see red, restore); unit tests open with `t.Parallel()` and stay under a second; a test file is never deleted (a file you empty keeps its package clause and one comment naming where its tests went). A Test that becomes a table row keeps its name as the row's. Report lines before and after for each file.

HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED. (1) Every behaviour a test pinned before is pinned after: count the checks (assert and require calls, table rows) before and after, and break three of the behaviours in the code on purpose to see the tests go red, then restore. (2) Production code changes only where a step says, and never its output. (3) No sleep, timer wait, socket, real clock or `t.Setenv` is added to a unit test; every test touched opens with `t.Parallel()`. (4) Test names are kept unless a step says otherwise (a Test that becomes a table row keeps its name as the row's). (5) Nothing outside PATHS and NEW.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names (cd <that path>) and run git log --oneline -1: the head is 36f4c5ba6371 or a later commit of BASE. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/gocache GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Sites and counts here were read at 36f4c5ba6371: find a moved line by its text.
STEP 2. (hard) compact 3 test files of internal/record.
