  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
Compact the tests in ledger_functional_test.go (433), ledger_server_functional_test.go (142), ledger_test.go (154) of `internal/record` (729 lines).
STEP 3. Read `git diff -U0` from the start commit against HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED, hunk by hunk; fix in the step that owns the hunk.
STEP 4. Run the gate once, each line as written, keeping each last line: `gofmt -l internal/record   (prints nothing)` ; `nice -n 19 go vet ./internal/record/` ; `nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/record/ ./internal/ci/`. If a test in ./internal/ci/ fails naming a ledger row (\"delete the stale entry\", \"below allowed count\", \"shrink the count\", \"lower the row\"), run `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1 nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '<the failing tests, joined with |>'`, then the gate again. Keep only the ledger lines of files PATHS names and the shards internal/ci/testdata/<ledger>/<package>.txt of its packages; restore any other it rewrote; name a needed one (partial). A row only shrinks. Not yours: TestGeneralityText red on two stale SPEC-BUS-DELIVERY.md rows (dead-generality-text-t2 deletes them).
