`inbox` reads a stale checkout and says nothing (a cold user: after another participant pushed a note to the remote, `nova-bus inbox --bus <checkout> --as Ada` listed the old state and printed no word that the checkout was behind). The inbox either fetches first (it already fetches on --advance) or says it did not: add a fact `fetched=false behind=unknown` and a NOTE with the command that brings the checkout level (`run: nova-bus inbox ... --fetch` or the existing verb that fetches). Decide which by reading the verb's help promise and docs/SPEC-BUS.md; the test runs over a bare remote in t.TempDir() (functional tag if it needs git).
STEP 3. (hard) advance bodies.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-bus/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-bus.txt, internal/bus/*.go
  COMMIT: use-bus-t: advance bodies
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
`inbox --advance --bodies` with nothing new neither advances nor says so (a cold user: exit 0, no word). The result says what happened: `advanced=false reason=nothing-new` (or advances, if the spec says it should): read docs/SPEC-BUS.md's cursor rules first and follow them. A test pins both cases.
