  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
Flags after a file are refused (`nova-self-talk draft.md --json` gives `flags come before files`), where nova-memory takes them anywhere (docs/STANDARD.md: one shape across the set). Accept flags anywhere among the files (stop at `--`). A test.
STEP 4. line order.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-self-talk/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-self-talk.txt
  COMMIT: use-self-talk-t: line order
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
Findings print grouped by class, not in line order (`I am the best.` on line 1 and `I am bad at x.` on line 2 print line 2 first). Sort findings by file, then line, then column. A test.
STEP 5. skip nomatch.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-self-talk/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-self-talk.txt
  COMMIT: use-self-talk-t: skip nomatch
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
`--skip` and `--rule-doc` with a basename that matches nothing are accepted silently. Print a NOTE naming each that matched nothing. A test.
