PATHS: cmd/nova-check/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-check.txt, internal/check/*.go
TEST: cmd/nova-check TestEveryPrintedArgumentIsLiteralQuotedOrEscaped
Deadline: finish within 60 minutes.

You are a child of the coordinator: one task, one checkout, one branch, unattended; this card is the whole task. You start in the job directory (export JOB=$PWD): read $JOB/JOB.md first, work in the staged checkout it names (a full clone at BASE), commit as usual and finish as it says. No gh, no push: JOB.md's finish does both.
Libraries considered: the standard library (strings, slices, maps, errors, io/fs, os, time passed in as a value), the tree's internal/tool (Out, Call.Problem, the refusal grammar), internal/oneline (ShellWord, Field, Quote) and internal/testkit, and testify for tests; nothing third-party is added, and a helper over thirty lines is written only after the PR body names what was searched first.
The contract is docs/STANDARD.md (embedded in AGENTS.md): read the sections a step names first; where this card and it disagree, it wins and the PR body says so.
Steps marked (hard) were dealt pro in the flat wave and may need pro; the card is dealt flash first and the machine escalates, never you.

THE TASK. A tree of 3 work steps (STEP 2 to STEP 4), walked in order. Each work step carries its own PATHS:, COMMIT: and VERDICT: lines: do it, run its check, commit only its PATHS with its COMMIT: line as the message, and write its verdict line in the PR body and RESULT, `step <n>: <ok|broken|not-done|skipped> <the full 40-hex commit sha pasted from git rev-parse HEAD, or - when nothing changed; a short sha is refused: e.g. step 2: ok 3b1f0c2a9d4e7f6a5c8b1d0e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f90 the change> <one line>` (ok with `-` and the commit that did it when the head already holds the step). The first step that is not ok stops the walk: steps before it land, and the coordinator turns the rest into a new card. What cold users proved by running the tool (docs/STANDARD.md sections 2 and 3). Each step: reproduce the defect first (build the tool into $JOB: `go build -o $JOB/bin/ ./cmd/<tool>/`) and keep the output for the PR body; write the test first in a `_test.go` of the package, named for what it pins (`t.Parallel()`, testify, no socket, no sleep, no real clock), see it red; make the smallest change that turns it green; lower the tool's tool-answers row where a step clears it.

HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED. (1) Each step's change is the one the step names and no other: every +/- line of `git diff -U0` traces to one sentence of its step. (2) Behaviour no step names is unchanged: the package's existing tests pass unedited, except an expected line a step itself changes. (3) A new behaviour has a test that fails before the change and passes after (write it first, see it red), named for what it pins, opening with `t.Parallel()`, in testify. (4) A printed event prefix or field name that docs/TESTS.md shows is kept: add a field, never rename one, unless the step says so. (5) A refusal names what the input wants and the command to run next, in the skeleton's grammar (`VERB REFUSED: <why>; run: <remedy>`). (6) Nothing is guessed: where the code cannot tell what is right, the PR body says so and the step ends partial.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names (cd <that path>) and run git log --oneline -1: the head is 36f4c5ba6371 or a later commit of BASE. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/gocache GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Sites and counts here were read at 36f4c5ba6371: find a moved line by its text.
STEP 2. (hard) links anchors.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-check/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-check.txt, internal/check/*.go
  COMMIT: use-check-2-t: links anchors
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
`links` says every relative markdown link resolves, and passes `[bad anchor](docs/X.md#nope)` (a cold user). Check the fragment against the target file's headings (GitHub's anchor rule: lower-case, spaces to dashes, punctuation dropped) and report a missing anchor as a finding with file:line; a link to a non-markdown file keeps no anchor check. Table tests in internal/check.
STEP 3. spelling scope.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-check/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-check.txt
  COMMIT: use-check-2-t: spelling scope
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
`spelling` says it checks prose for misspellings but is a list of known misspellings (`mesage` passed, `Teh` was caught). Say so in its help line and the docs line: \"checks against a list of common misspellings; it is not a dictionary\". No behaviour change.
STEP 4. spelling column.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-check/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-check.txt, internal/check/*.go
  COMMIT: use-check-2-t: spelling column
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
`spelling` reports `memory/a.md:3:0`: the line counts from 1 and the column from 0. Count the column from 1, as editors do. A test.
STEP 5. Read `git diff -U0` from the start commit against HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED, hunk by hunk; fix in the step that owns the hunk.
STEP 6. Run the gate once, each line as written, keeping each last line: `gofmt -l cmd/nova-check internal/check   (prints nothing)` ; `nice -n 19 go vet ./cmd/nova-check/ ./internal/check/` ; `nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./cmd/nova-check/ ./internal/check/ ./internal/ci/`. If a test in ./internal/ci/ fails naming a ledger row (\"delete the stale entry\", \"below allowed count\", \"shrink the count\", \"lower the row\"), run `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1 nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '<the failing tests, joined with |>'`, then the gate again. Keep only the ledger lines of files PATHS names and the shards internal/ci/testdata/<ledger>/<package>.txt of its packages; restore any other it rewrote; name a needed one (partial). A row only shrinks. Not yours: TestGeneralityText red on two stale SPEC-BUS-DELIVERY.md rows (dead-generality-text-t2 deletes them).
STEP 7. The pull request: title `use-check-2-t: links anchors and 2 more steps`; the body gives the diff stat, what was deleted, each step's verdict line, the gate lines with their last lines, each test added and what it pins, the three measures of docs/STANDARD.md (minimal: lines before and after; performant: a number the gate prints; correct: the test or model holding the behaviour) and what was not done, and ends with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.
STEP 8. End as JOB.md says: its `gh pr create` is the end, or RESULT.md in JOB.md's shape (head, branch, verdict, gate, output, report, and the step lines); never a green claim.

AS A READ (only when JOB.md's first line is `# JOB: read <card>, attempt <n>`; otherwise you are the work): change nothing; diff from the start commit JOB.md names. THE GATE PROVES: the tools build, vet and pass with the new tests, the docs and class tests pass, and the tool-answers rows fell. Run it once (STEP 6). READ ONLY: for each step, the defect shows when you run the step's command at the start commit and not at the head; revert the step's non-test hunks and its test goes red. And: only PATHS, NEW and STEP 6's ledger lines changed; a deleted test has its deleted-tests.txt row; one commit per work step. Approve (`gh pr review --approve`) only when all hold, else `gh pr review --request-changes --body <file:line and what is wrong>`.

RULES.
Work only in the staged checkout JOB.md names; do not clone.
Commit on the checkout's own branch, as usual; touch no other branch.
Export a private GOCACHE (the path this card names) and GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command.
Never `go clean`, and never clean a shared cache.
NEVER start a redis-server on this machine.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Every `go test` gets `-timeout 600s`.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Never force-push.
Never rebase.
Do not use git stash (the stash list is shared by every worktree).
Functional tests (any test that needs Redis) run ONLY inside the container through `tools/functionalrun` (`--fresh-gocache --deadline 15m`), never against any other store.
Every new test opens with `t.Parallel()`.
Run `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/` before you finish.
No names of people, machines or friends in code, comments or docs.
Docs and comments in the present tense.
Cite the model or the design section from every function that implements a rule.
Touch only the files this card names; a fix that needs another file goes into your report as a proposed diff, not a commit.
Keep the diff minimal: every added line traceable to one sentence of this card.
Commit messages end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude <your model> <noreply@anthropic.com>`. Commits may use the machine's git identity for now, but every commit body carries a line `By: <who did the work>` above the Co-Authored-By trailer: the friend's name for a friend card (By: Rowan, By: Emma, ...), the route's model name for a fleet child (e.g. By: deepseek-v4.1-flash).
PR bodies end with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.
Finish as JOB.md says, with `gh pr create` against the base this card names; never merge.
The PR body states the diff stat and what was deleted.
The PR body lists the tests, each with what it pins, and every local helper added.
The report is the PR: its title is the one-line report, its body every test package line and what you could not do and why.
\"Not done\" is a welcome report; a green claim you did not run is not.
A card that builds code carries a filled line `Libraries considered: <what the standard library and the adopted modules offered, and why each was used or not>` (docs/STANDARD.md section 7).
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never start a server on this machine.
Report what was not done.")
