Four release verbs refuse the version their own help gives as the example (a cold user). Make each help's example a version the verb accepts (or the verb accept the documented form), and run every help example in a test.
STEP 3. (hard) release help per verb.
  PATHS: internal/release/*.go, cmd/nova-update/main.go, internal/update/cli.go
  COMMIT: use-release-t: release help per verb
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
`help release` is 6.4 KB of unbroken prose under five usage lines (a cold user); the --dry-run forms are there and not findable. Give each release verb its own `-h` with its effect and its dry run, and move the reference prose to help topics (the skeleton's Topics) after the move to nova-release.
STEP 4. Read `git diff -U0` from the start commit against HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED, hunk by hunk; fix in the step that owns the hunk.
STEP 5. Run the gate once, each line as written, keeping each last line: `gofmt -l internal/release cmd/nova-update internal/update   (prints nothing)` ; `nice -n 19 go vet ./internal/release/ ./cmd/nova-update/ ./internal/update/` ; `nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/release/ ./cmd/nova-update/ ./internal/update/ ./internal/ci/`. If a test in ./internal/ci/ fails naming a ledger row (\"delete the stale entry\", \"below allowed count\", \"shrink the count\", \"lower the row\"), run `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1 nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '<the failing tests, joined with |>'`, then the gate again. Keep only the ledger lines of files PATHS names and the shards internal/ci/testdata/<ledger>/<package>.txt of its packages; restore any other it rewrote; name a needed one (partial). A row only shrinks. Not yours: TestGeneralityText red on two stale SPEC-BUS-DELIVERY.md rows (dead-generality-text-t2 deletes them).
