A second `lockdown` (or a `quarantine` of the same surface) silently replaces the recorded time and reason (a cold user). The first blow stands: a repeat with the same reason is `already=true` and keeps the original time; a repeat with another reason is refused naming the recorded one, with the remedy (`nova-fuse help lift lockdown` for how a blown fuse is replaced). Tests.
STEP 3. (hard) extra words.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-fuse/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-fuse.txt
  COMMIT: use-fuse-t: extra words
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
Extra words are joined into the reason, so a second surface becomes prose (`quarantine a.example b.example \"why\"` records one surface and the reason \"b.example why\"). Refuse more positional words than the verb takes, naming them, with the quoted form as the remedy. A test.
STEP 4. lift remedy.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-fuse/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-fuse.txt
  COMMIT: use-fuse-t: lift remedy
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
The `lift lockdown` refusal says a blown fuse \"is REPLACED\" and does not point at `nova-fuse help lift lockdown`, the one place that says how. End the refusal with `run: nova-fuse help lift lockdown`. A test.
STEP 5. (hard) dry run.
