Zero-score hits print as hits (`rank=2 score=0.00`, `rank=3 score=0.00`). Stop at the last hit above zero and say `hits=1 k=3`. A test.
STEP 3. (hard) frontmatter.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-memory/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/nova-memory.txt, internal/memindex/*.go
  COMMIT: use-memory-3-t: frontmatter
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
Front matter is indexed as body text: a query on a key word matches and the snippet is mostly YAML (`search ... type project` returns `---\\nname: x\\ntype: project\\n---`). Index the body after a leading `---` front-matter block; keep the front matter out of snippets. A test.
STEP 4. Read `git diff -U0` from the start commit against HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED, hunk by hunk; fix in the step that owns the hunk.
STEP 5. Run the gate once, each line as written, keeping each last line: `gofmt -l cmd/nova-memory internal/memindex   (prints nothing)` ; `nice -n 19 go vet ./cmd/nova-memory/ ./internal/memindex/` ; `nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./cmd/nova-memory/ ./internal/memindex/ ./internal/ci/`. If a test in ./internal/ci/ fails naming a ledger row (\"delete the stale entry\", \"below allowed count\", \"shrink the count\", \"lower the row\"), run `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1 nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '<the failing tests, joined with |>'`, then the gate again. Keep only the ledger lines of files PATHS names and the shards internal/ci/testdata/<ledger>/<package>.txt of its packages; restore any other it rewrote; name a needed one (partial). A row only shrinks. Not yours: TestGeneralityText red on two stale SPEC-BUS-DELIVERY.md rows (dead-generality-text-t2 deletes them).
