For each row: give the test a per-test seam for the reason the row names (t.Setenv -> the child's cmd.Env or a field on the value under test; t.Chdir/os.Chdir -> cmd.Dir or a path argument; a swapped package var -> a field or parameter on the value under test, the package var kept only as the production default), open the test with t.Parallel() as its first statement, and delete its row. A test that needs a real process-wide resource and cannot be seamed goes to the functional tier instead (//go:build functional, its own file), and its row still goes. Finish inside the deadline: take the files in order, commit after each file, and if the deadline nears report the remaining rows as not-done, removing exactly the rows you fixed. Tier pro: a row that swaps a package var (or many rows) needs a per-test seam on the value under test (a field, a parameter, a clock or dialer injected), which is a design decision per test family. The ledger file is shared by every card of this ledger: remove only your own row(s) and change no other line of it (never a ceiling line); the lander resolves ledger conflicts.

STEP 1. Enter the staged checkout JOB.md names, no clone; inspect git status and the actual full head. Work only on its own branch. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any Go command. Scratch belongs under $JOB/scratch. Read AGENTS.md; cite the ledger's header comment from the change.
STEP 2. Make it red first: delete the row(s) of cmd/nova-sandbox from internal/ci/testdata/serial-tests_allowlist.txt (and nothing else there); TestEveryTestOpensWithTParallel is red because the tests still do not open with t.Parallel(). Run go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '^TestEveryTestOpensWithTParallel$' and keep the failing line as evidence.
STEP 3. Make it green by changing only the named PATHS, minimally: seam each test as above and open it with t.Parallel(); the class test and the package's own tests (with -race) are green. Commit the draft on your own branch as soon as the test is green, before any further probe; a later commit may refine it. A change any other file needs goes in the report as a proposed diff, never a commit.
STEP 4. Run the gate: go test -count=1 -race -timeout 600s ./cmd/nova-sandbox/ ./internal/ci/ and keep the last line of each. Run gofmt -l on every changed Go file; it must print nothing. No Redis or external service is needed; a functional test that needs Redis runs only through tools/functionalrun --fresh-gocache --deadline 15m, never a host store.
STEP 5. Inspect the diff and commit only the named files on your own branch. Present-tense comments and docs; no names of people, machines or friends. Commit trailer Co-Authored-By: Claude <your model> <noreply@anthropic.com>. Finish exactly through JOB.md's protocol, no direct external publication; the STEP3 SHA in RESULT.md is the exact 40-hex git rev-parse HEAD. Report the actual gates, the red-to-green evidence, the diff stat, and what was not done. PR body ends with 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code). Normal independent review is required before landing; never merge yourself.")))
