AS A READ (only when JOB.md's first line is `# JOB: read <card>, attempt <n>`; otherwise you are the work): change nothing; diff from the start commit JOB.md names. THE GATE PROVES: the packages build and pass (no code changed), the onboarding and docs tests pass, and the banner ledger rows fell. Run it once (STEP 4). READ ONLY: every changed sentence reads whole and is true of the code (for each reason given, find the line that shows it); every example line of a banner runs as printed in a temporary directory. And: only PATHS, NEW and STEP 4's ledger lines changed; a deleted test has its deleted-tests.txt row; one commit per work step. Approve (`gh pr review --approve`) only when all hold, else `gh pr review --request-changes --body <file:line and what is wrong>`.

