THE TASK. A tree of 4 work steps (STEP 2 to STEP 5), walked in order. Each work step carries its own PATHS:, COMMIT: and VERDICT: lines: do it, run its check, commit only its PATHS with its COMMIT: line as the message, and write its verdict line in the PR body and RESULT, `step <n>: <ok|broken|not-done|skipped> <the full 40-hex commit sha pasted from git rev-parse HEAD, or - when nothing changed; a short sha is refused: e.g. step 2: ok 3b1f0c2a9d4e7f6a5c8b1d0e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f90 the change> <one line>` (ok with `-` and the commit that did it when the head already holds the step). The first step that is not ok stops the walk: steps before it land, and the coordinator turns the rest into a new card. What cold readers found in the code (docs/STANDARD.md section 7: minimal and readable). Each step is one reading fix; behaviour unchanged unless the step says otherwise: the package's tests pass unedited.

HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED. (1) Each step's change is the one the step names and no other: every +/- line of `git diff -U0` traces to one sentence of its step. (2) Behaviour no step names is unchanged: the package's existing tests pass unedited, except an expected line a step itself changes. (3) A new behaviour has a test that fails before the change and passes after (write it first, see it red), named for what it pins, opening with `t.Parallel()`, in testify. (4) A printed event prefix or field name that docs/TESTS.md shows is kept: add a field, never rename one, unless the step says so. (5) A refusal names what the input wants and the command to run next, in the skeleton's grammar (`VERB REFUSED: <why>; run: <remedy>`). (6) Nothing is guessed: where the code cannot tell what is right, the PR body says so and the step ends partial.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names (cd <that path>) and run git log --oneline -1: the head is 36f4c5ba6371 or a later commit of BASE. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/gocache GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Sites and counts here were read at 36f4c5ba6371: find a moved line by its text.
STEP 2. index twice.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-cairn/*.go, internal/cairn/*.go
  COMMIT: read-cairn-t: index twice
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
`index` calls `cairn.Index` and then `cairn.Coverage`, which calls Index again: the store is walked twice, and Index's `max` parameter is always 0 from its one caller. Return the session count from one walk and drop `max`. Behaviour unchanged unless the task says otherwise: the package's tests pass unedited.
STEP 3. published fields.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-cairn/*.go, internal/cairn/*.go
  COMMIT: read-cairn-t: published fields
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
`AppendResult.Published` and `ReceiptInfo.Published` are never set, and main.go hard-codes `published=false`. Cut the fields, keep the printed fact. Behaviour unchanged unless the task says otherwise: the package's tests pass unedited.
STEP 4. small hand rolls.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-cairn/*.go, internal/cairn/*.go
  COMMIT: read-cairn-t: small hand rolls
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
Small hand-rolls (a cold reader): `cmpOr` and `sourceOf` are `cmp.Or`; `appendBytes` and `appendLine` differ by one flag (one function with the flag); \"no store given; refusing to guess\" is written four times for a case main.go already refuses (keep the one in main). Behaviour unchanged unless the task says otherwise: the package's tests pass unedited.
STEP 5. (hard) open remedy.
  PATHS: internal/cairn/*.go
  COMMIT: read-cairn-t: open remedy
  VERDICT: ok when the step's change is made and its package's tests pass; not-done or broken naming what remains
internal/cairn/open_remedy.go builds a remedy that emits an octal-decoding subshell for control characters in a store path: 58 lines of cleverness for a case a refusal serves (\"this path cannot be printed as one line; rename it\"), with a second copy of a shell quoter. Replace it with that refusal and oneline.ShellWord. A test. Behaviour unchanged unless the task says otherwise: the package's tests pass unedited.
STEP 6. Read `git diff -U0` from the start commit against HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED, hunk by hunk; fix in the step that owns the hunk.
STEP 7. Run the gate once, each line as written, keeping each last line: `gofmt -l cmd/nova-cairn internal/cairn   (prints nothing)` ; `nice -n 19 go vet ./cmd/nova-cairn/ ./internal/cairn/` ; `nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./cmd/nova-cairn/ ./internal/cairn/ ./internal/ci/`. If a test in ./internal/ci/ fails naming a ledger row (\"delete the stale entry\", \"below allowed count\", \"shrink the count\", \"lower the row\"), run `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1 nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '<the failing tests, joined with |>'`, then the gate again. Keep only the ledger lines of files PATHS names and the shards internal/ci/testdata/<ledger>/<package>.txt of its packages; restore any other it rewrote; name a needed one (partial). A row only shrinks. Not yours: TestGeneralityText red on two stale SPEC-BUS-DELIVERY.md rows (dead-generality-text-t2 deletes them).
STEP 8. The pull request: title `read-cairn-t: index twice and 3 more steps`; the body gives the diff stat, what was deleted, each step's verdict line, the gate lines with their last lines, each test added and what it pins, the three measures of docs/STANDARD.md (minimal: lines before and after; performant: a number the gate prints; correct: the test or model holding the behaviour) and what was not done, and ends with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.
STEP 9. End as JOB.md says: its `gh pr create` is the end, or RESULT.md in JOB.md's shape (head, branch, verdict, gate, output, report, and the step lines); never a green claim.

AS A READ (only when JOB.md's first line is `# JOB: read <card>, attempt <n>`; otherwise you are the work): change nothing; diff from the start commit JOB.md names. THE GATE PROVES: the packages build, vet and pass unedited, and the class tests pass. Run it once (STEP 7). READ ONLY: each step's change makes the code read as the step says and changes no printed line. And: only PATHS, NEW and STEP 7's ledger lines changed; a deleted test has its deleted-tests.txt row; one commit per work step. Approve (`gh pr review --approve`) only when all hold, else `gh pr review --request-changes --body <file:line and what is wrong>`.

RULES.
