     ((:id "fg-session-broken-on-provider-refusal" :tier "-" :needs ("fg-delivery-no-progress-not-a-cap")
      :title "A broken session is noticed, said once, and not fed"
      :brief "RESULT: fg-session-broken-on-provider-refusal sha=3f26f822126b tier: pro
REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: rowan/integration-2026-10-04
KIND: fix-red
DEPENDS-ON: fg-delivery-no-progress-not-a-cap
PATHS: internal/friend/adapter.go,internal/friend/adapter_test.go,internal/friend/daemon.go,internal/friend/daemon_test.go,internal/friend/state.go,internal/friend/state_test.go,internal/friend/machine.go,cmd/nova-friend/main.go,cmd/nova-friend/main_test.go,docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md,docs/CLI.md,tla/README.md,tla/RUNS.tsv,tla/CASES.tsv
NEW: tla/Delivery.tla,tla/MCDelivery.tla,tla/MCDelivery.cfg,tla/MCDeliveryBrokenTwoTurns.cfg,tla/MCDeliveryBrokenDeliverWhileBroken.cfg,tla/MCDeliveryBrokenDeferralCounts.cfg
TEST: ./internal/friend TestARepeatedProviderRefusalMarksTheSessionBroken
Deadline: finish within 120 minutes.
You are a child of the coordinator: one task, one staged checkout, one branch, unattended. This card is the whole task. Read $JOB/JOB.md first. Start at the current BASE tip; admission inspected exact base 3f26f822126bda57b104b7049e9a3efa2d799560. Verify the gap still exists before editing; if it is already done, report not-done with exact evidence rather than duplicate work. One change, tests that are red before and green after. Write the draft early and commit it before any extra probe.
Libraries considered: the tree's own packages (internal/friend, its adapters and its fake Exec) and testify; no new dependency. Counts toward nova-tools v1.2.0 (stream friends-general-v1-2-0). Glenn, 2026-10-04 ~1:00 PM ET: friends reliably talking with each other ship in nova-tools, through nova-bus and nova-friend, not opinionated only in nova-sprint; nova-sprint only consumes them. Every line this card adds passes one test: someone who never runs nova-sprint uses it as it is. A stranger with their own AIs must be able to do this from nova-tools and its docs alone; no Studio paths, names or our friends in the tool (Glenn, 2026-10-04 1:14 PM ET: 'everything we are doing inside nova-sprint and working with friends, other people can do too with their own AIs, using nova-tools ideally').

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.

THE TASK. A broken session is noticed, said once, and not fed. Measured 2026-10-04: Freddy's OpenCode session (Mercury 2.5) rejected every turn with the provider's `invalid_request_error` from 11:22 AM; his daemon kept delivering, every turn failed, the failed turns piled up in the session, and the friends table showed him up and working 8 the whole time.
The rule:
- Each adapter classifies a failed delivery from its exit code and output: a provider refusal (the provider's error type in the harness's output: `invalid_request_error`, an authentication or permission error, out of credit or funds, HTTP 400/401/402/403 from the provider; the patterns are data per harness, beside the adapter) versus any other failure. Three provider refusals in a row from one session (BrokenAfter = 3, the same patterns, no success between) mark the session broken. A rate limit (429) is not broken: it defers.
- Broken: the daemon delivers nothing more into that session (messages stay pending, never acked, never counted toward given_up); it sends ONE bus message to its coordinator, subject `session broken: <friend>`, body the refusal line, first seen, count and the remedy (`fix the session, then: nova-friend reset --as <friend> --dir <d>`); `nova-friend status` says `broken=<RFC3339> reason=<line>` and exits 1; the daemon's presence carries `broken` and `reason` (read by fg-presence-off-the-sprint-server, which shows the friend down with the reason). The mark is in the state file, so a restart keeps it.
- Cleared by `nova-friend reset --as <me> --dir <d> [--json]` (new verb: `RESET OK broken=false`, exit 0; `RESET NONE` at exit 1 when nothing was marked), or by the session's own `pong --nonce` (the session proved it takes turns); the next delivery then goes.
- The failed-delivery counts move into the state file in the same change, so a restart neither forgets a poison message's count nor resets a broken mark (the missed-15 finding; that card is on the wrong base, and this card does it).
GENERAL: what this card adds imports no internal/sprint*, internal/nsprint* or internal/sprintwire package, says no sprint word in help or docs, and waits on no sprint server.
Unit tests use no real time and open no socket: an injected clock (or testing/synctest) and the package's fake store; the logic is a function apart from its transport (a server is a function of its input, a client takes a send function). Every new test opens with t.Parallel(), in testify. A test that needs Redis is functional (-tags functional) and runs only through tools/functionalrun --fresh-gocache --deadline 15m, never against a store on this machine.
Usable cold by an AI from the tool's help alone: the verb's help names every flag, every output line and JSON field, every exit code, and one example that runs as written; docs/CLI.md carries the same text; the verbhelp tests pin it.
Tests, with a fake Exec printing the measured refusal and a fake clock: TestARepeatedProviderRefusalMarksTheSessionBroken (three refusals: broken, one coordinator message, no fourth delivery), TestARateLimitDefersAndIsNotBroken, TestBrokenSurvivesARestart (the state file), TestResetClearsBrokenAndTheNextDeliveryGoes, TestTheSessionsOwnPongClearsBroken, TestFailedCountsSurviveARestart.
TLA+ (the delivery machine; states pending, delivering, deferred, delivered, given-up per message, and ok, busy, broken per session): tla/Delivery.tla with tla/MCDelivery.tla and tla/MCDelivery.cfg. Invariants: at most one message delivering per session; nothing delivering while the session is broken; a message is acked only delivered or given up; given up only after MaxDeliveries failures that were neither deferrals nor refusals of a broken session; a restart (an action that keeps only the state file) changes none of these. Broken configs, each failing one invariant: MCDeliveryBrokenTwoTurns, MCDeliveryBrokenDeliverWhileBroken, MCDeliveryBrokenDeferralCounts. TLC on a small instance on a bench machine, never the Studio; rows in tla/RUNS.tsv and tla/CASES.tsv; every counterexample checked against the code by hand. SPEC-FRIEND: the loop section names the model and the broken rule; CLI.md and help: reset, and status's broken line.

