THE TASK. The friend health check as a verb. Glenn, 2026-10-04 1:12 PM ET: \"this stuff you are doing now should probably be formalized into nova-friend tool\". The coordinator ran this by hand today; this card makes it a verb any coordinator of friends uses, with no nova-sprint. The hand version (/private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-nova-ai-rowan-working-rowan-new/901c251c-bab9-45eb-b5d6-405e58a50100/scratchpad/friendcheck.sh; read it first) reads, per friend: the launchd agent's arguments and pid, `nova-friend status`, the RUN lines of the daemon's log (last result, failures in the last 20, deferrals, given_up), the bus log (real messages from the friend in the last 30 minutes, the last one), the friend's newest outbox entry, and the sprint's friends row; then the coordinator judges by eye whether the row is true. Make it one verb whose verdict is the judgment:
- `nova-friend check [--as <coordinator>] [<friend>...] [--since <duration>] [--shown <file|->] [--json]`. The friends are the arguments, else every presence record. `--shown` is what some consumer shows of each friend, as JSON `{\"<friend>\":{\"state\":\"up|asleep|down\",\"working\":n}}` (a sprint passes its friends table through it; nova-friend reads no sprint).
- Per friend, lines in this order: `CHECK DAEMON friend=<f> agent=<loaded|not-loaded|none> pid=<n|-> status=<ok|stale|none> connection=<..> challenge=<..> pong_age=<s|-> presence=<up|asleep|down> seen_age=<s|->`; `CHECK HARNESS friend=<f> harness=<h> route=<push|defer|passive> last=<RFC3339|-> last_exit=<n|-> failed_of_last20=<n> deferred=<n> broken=<RFC3339|-> reason=<line|->`; `CHECK BUS friend=<f> real_since=<n> last_real=<RFC3339|->` (real: not ping, pong, daemon-pong or keepalive); `CHECK WORK friend=<f> inbox=<n> outbox=<n> newest_outbox=<name|-> newest_at=<RFC3339|->` (the friend's inbox/ and outbox/ under its directory, when present); then `CHECK VERDICT friend=<f> verdict=<ok|broken|silent|deaf|down|untrue> shown=<state/working|-> why=<one line>`.
- The verdict is a pure function of the facts (its rules cited from SPEC-FRIEND \"Check\"): broken when the session is marked broken or every delivery in the window failed; deaf when deliveries succeed but no session pong or real message came back in the window; silent when no delivery was due and nothing came back; down by presence; untrue when `--shown` says up or working and the facts say otherwise (the measured case: \"shown up/working 8, no turn answered since 11:22 AM: broken\"); else ok.
- Summary `CHECK OK friends=<n> ok=<n> broken=<n> deaf=<n> silent=<n> down=<n> untrue=<n>`. Exit 0 when every verdict is ok, 1 when any is not (a check that found something), 2 when it could not run. `--json` carries the same facts per friend and the verdicts.
The facts are gathered through seams (launchctl, the status file, the log file, the bus store, the directory listing: each an injected func); the verdict is a function; tests use fakes only.
