ATTRIBUTION. Commits end with the trailer Co-Authored-By: Claude <model> <noreply@anthropic.com> as nova-tools AGENTS.md and docs/STANDARD.md require, naming the actual model; reports identify Rowan and the harness; the PR footer is the one those documents name. Commits may use the machine's git identity for now, but every commit body carries a line `By: <who did the work>` above the Co-Authored-By trailer: the friend's name for a friend card (By: Rowan, By: Emma, ...), the route's model name for a fleet child (e.g. By: deepseek-v4.1-flash).

You are a friend of the coordinator, and this card is one sprint job (docs/FRIENDS.md), delivered as `~/rowan-working/inbox/<job>/BRIEF.md`: its STATUS line names the epoch, attempt and branch to push. Work only under `~/rowan-working/jobs/<job>/`, using `~/rowan-working/.cache/go-build`. In this card, JOB.md means the delivered BRIEF.md. Admission inspected the exact base 3f26f822126bda57b104b7049e9a3efa2d799560; start at the current tip of origin/rowan/integration-2026-10-04.

THE TASK. A broken session gets a fresh one in the same harness, as a verb. Glenn, 2026-10-04 1:12 PM ET: \"this stuff you are doing now should probably be formalized into nova-friend tool\". The coordinator ran this by hand today; this card makes it a verb any coordinator of friends uses, with no nova-sprint. Measured: Freddy's OpenCode session (Mercury 2.5) refused every turn with the provider's invalid_request_error from 11:22 AM; the fix by hand is a new session in the same harness and directory, told who it is and why.
- `nova-friend renew --as <coordinator> <friend> [--reason <text>] [--dry-run] [--json]`: reads the friend's daemon state (harness, directory, pinned session); starts a fresh session in the SAME harness and directory through the harness's own command for a new session (OpenCode: a new session id; Codex, DSH, Grok, Antigravity: their new-chat route where the open-chat cards found one; a harness with none is refused with the reason, nothing changed); seeds it with one first turn, the wake brief: the friend's own identity files under its directory (AGENTS.md and memory/ when present: named, never copied into the bus), the old session id, why it was renewed (the broken reason or --reason), and the pong line; re-pins the daemon to the new session (the state file and, when installed, the agent's --session) and restarts the daemon; clears the broken mark. The old session is never deleted or edited.
- Lines: `RENEW NEW friend=<f> harness=<h> old=<id> new=<id>`, `RENEW SEEDED friend=<f> bytes=<n>`, `RENEW PINNED friend=<f> session=<id>`, then `RENEW OK friend=<f> old=<id> new=<id>` exit 0; `RENEW REFUSED` with the remedy exit 1; 2 could not run. `--dry-run` prints the commands it would run. `--json` the same facts.
- Every harness command goes through the Exec seam; tests use a fake Exec.
MEASURED: renew the live broken session if one still exists when this runs (else a throwaway OpenCode session in a scratch directory under the job), then a real bus message to the friend is answered by the new session's own bus line within 60 s; the lines in the report.
GENERAL: what this card adds imports no internal/sprint*, internal/nsprint* or internal/sprintwire package, says no sprint word in help or docs, and waits on no sprint server.
Unit tests use no real time and open no socket: an injected clock (or testing/synctest) and the package's fake store; the logic is a function apart from its transport (a server is a function of its input, a client takes a send function). Every new test opens with t.Parallel(), in testify. A test that needs Redis is functional (-tags functional) and runs only through tools/functionalrun --fresh-gocache --deadline 15m, never against a store on this machine.
Usable cold by an AI from the tool's help alone: the verb's help names every flag, every output line and JSON field, every exit code, and one example that runs as written; docs/CLI.md carries the same text; the verbhelp tests pin it.
Tests: TestRenewStartsAFreshSessionAndRepinsTheDaemon, TestRenewNeverTouchesTheOldSession, TestRenewRefusesAHarnessWithNoNewSessionRoute, TestRenewSeedNamesTheIdentityFilesTheOldSessionAndTheReason, TestRenewDryRunChangesNothing. SPEC-FRIEND: a section \"Renew\" (per harness: the new-session command). CLI.md and help: renew.

