THE TASK. One uniform push into the OPEN chat of any terminal harness (OpenCode, Grok, Aider, any TUI) when it is hosted in tmux: the friend's session is the TUI in the pane, the daemon types into it exactly as a person would, and a person can attach and watch. Glenn, 2026-10-04 1:10 PM ET: the coordinator may run terminal friends itself. Hosting is opt-in: a TUI a person launched outside tmux keeps its own harness adapter.
Contract:
- `nova-friend host --as <name> --harness <h> --dir <d> [--prompt <regexp>] [--dry-run] [--json] -- <launch command...>`: starts the command in a new detached tmux session named `friend-<name>` in `<d>` (`tmux new-session -d -s friend-<name> -c <d> -- <command...>`), refuses when that session exists (`HOST REFUSED: friend-<name> runs already; run: tmux attach -t friend-<name>`), and prints `HOST OK session=friend-<name> dir=<d> attach=\"tmux attach -t friend-<name>\"`. The harness's idle prompt pattern is data per harness (OpenCode, Grok, Aider to start; `--prompt` overrides); the session name and pattern are saved in the friend's state so `run` and `install` need no flag. Exit 0 started, 1 refused, 2 could not run.
- Harness `tmux` for `run`/`install` (or `--harness <h> --host tmux`, whichever the adapter registry takes more simply; say which): Deliver captures the pane (`tmux capture-pane -p -t friend-<name>`), and when its last non-empty line matches the idle prompt, types the text literally (`tmux send-keys -t friend-<name> -l <text>`, then `tmux send-keys -t friend-<name> Enter` as a second call), and is accepted once the prompt line has gone (the turn started), polled each half second for up to a minute; while the prompt is absent a turn runs and Deliver returns Deferred, and `Busy` (fg-delivery-no-progress-not-a-cap) says busy, so no second turn ever lands beside one. A missing tmux session is Deferred with the remedy (`nova-friend host ...`), never a failure count. Text with newlines is typed as one line, each newline shown as ` ⏎ `, as the Grok adapter does.
- The last screen of a hosted friend is the verb `nova-friend screen` (card fg-friend-screen-verb), not this card.
All tmux calls go through the package's Exec seam: the adapter is a function of captured screens and a clock.
GENERAL: what this card adds imports no internal/sprint*, internal/nsprint* or internal/sprintwire package, says no sprint word in help or docs, and waits on no sprint server.
Unit tests use no real time and open no socket: an injected clock (or testing/synctest) and the package's fake store; the logic is a function apart from its transport (a server is a function of its input, a client takes a send function). Every new test opens with t.Parallel(), in testify. A test that needs Redis is functional (-tags functional) and runs only through tools/functionalrun --fresh-gocache --deadline 15m, never against a store on this machine.
Usable cold by an AI from the tool's help alone: the verb's help names every flag, every output line and JSON field, every exit code, and one example that runs as written; docs/CLI.md carries the same text; the verbhelp tests pin it.
Tests, a fake Exec replaying captured screens and recording tmux argv, a fake clock: TestTmuxTypesIntoAnIdlePaneAndDefersDuringATurn, TestTmuxAcceptsOnceThePromptLineIsGone, TestTmuxMissingSessionDefersWithTheHostLine, TestHostRefusesASessionThatRuns, TestHostDryRunPrintsTheTmuxCommand. One functional test (tools/functionalrun, tmux in the container if present, else skipped with the reason) hosts `cat` behind a fake prompt and sees a typed line arrive. SPEC-FRIEND: a section \"Hosted in tmux\" (host, the idle rule, the screen, what a person runs to watch); CLI.md and help: host and the tmux harness. TLA+: the per-session busy and idle states are the delivery model's (fg-session-broken-on-provider-refusal's tla/Delivery.tla); say in the PR which action the pane's prompt drives.

STEP 1. Enter the staged checkout JOB.md names, no clone; inspect git status and the actual full head. Work only on its own branch. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any Go command. Scratch belongs under $JOB/scratch. Read AGENTS.md and the governing spec section; cite it from every function that implements a rule.
STEP 2. Write the red tests first, TestTmuxTypesIntoAnIdlePaneAndDefersDuringATurn among them, each opening with t.Parallel(). Run them and keep the failing lines as evidence.
STEP 3. Make them pass by changing only the named PATHS and NEW files, minimally. Commit the draft on your own branch as soon as the tests are green, before any further probe; a later commit may refine it. A change any other file needs goes in the report as a proposed diff, never a commit.
STEP 4. Run the gate: nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/friend/ ./cmd/nova-friend/ ./internal/ci/, and keep the last line of each. Run gofmt -l on every changed Go file; it must print nothing.
STEP 5. Inspect the diff and commit only the named files on your own branch. Present-tense comments and docs; no names of people, machines or friends. Commit trailer Co-Authored-By: Claude <your model> <noreply@anthropic.com>. Finish exactly through JOB.md's protocol, no direct external publication; the STEP3 SHA in RESULT.md is the exact 40-hex git rev-parse HEAD. Report the actual gates, the red-to-green evidence, the diff stat and deletions, every helper added, and what was not done. PR body ends with 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code). Normal independent review is required before landing; never merge yourself.")
