Libraries considered: TLA+ and TLC as the tree already uses them (tla/, tla/RUNS.tsv); no new dependency. Heavy work on the pro tier (the tier line takes flash|pro). Counts toward nova-tools v1.2.0 (stream friends-general-v1-2-0). Zhi gets this card because she modelled the friend liveness in tla/Friend.tla.

ATTRIBUTION: commits and reports name the friend (By: Zhi) and your actual model and harness. Never claim a model or harness you are not running. A Claude worker writes the true Claude trailer.

You are a friend of the coordinator, and this card is one sprint job (docs/FRIENDS.md), delivered as `~/zhi-working/inbox/<job>/BRIEF.md`: its STATUS line names the epoch, attempt and branch to push. Work only under `~/zhi-working/jobs/<job>/`. In this card, JOB.md means the delivered BRIEF.md.

THE TASK. Extend tla/Friend.tla (your liveness model) with the new delivery states that PR 5317 (rowan/friend-e2e, head 0e0212ad8, carried by this card's BASE rowan/integration-2026-10-04) built in internal/friend (daemon.go, lanes.go, the adapters). Read the code first, then model what it does:
  (a) batch delivery with one ack: several messages delivered in one turn, acknowledged once;
  (b) answered pings are never delivered as messages;
  (c) the silent stop: a turn that stops printing ends by the silence rule, with no fixed kill time;
  (d) a broken session: after K identical refusals the session is marked broken and receives no further delivery;
  (e) one-shot lanes: each lane waits for its card's RESULT.md; a card with none after two turns is set aside.
Invariants: no message is lost or acked unread; no two turns run on one session at once; a broken session receives no delivery. Keep the existing liveness properties. Reversed witnesses: for each invariant, a MCFriendBroken<Name>.cfg that breaks it on purpose must fail under TLC (as the existing MCFriendBroken*.cfg do), and the main MCFriend.cfg must pass. Check each counterexample against the code by hand before writing it down; if the model finds a real defect in the code, write it in the report as a finding with file:line (the code is not in PATHS; the coordinator cards the fix).
Run TLC on hetzner (the bench), never on the Studio, small instance (K=2, two lanes, two messages). Add one RUNS row per run to tla/RUNS.tsv in the file's existing format (states, distinct, depth, seconds, result).

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/zhi-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of origin/rowan/integration-2026-10-04. Read AGENTS.md, tla/Friend.tla, its MC files and RUNS.tsv, and internal/friend/{daemon.go,lanes.go} first.

STEP 2. Do the task above.
  PATHS: tla/Friend.tla,tla/MCFriend.tla,tla/MCFriend*.cfg,tla/RUNS.tsv
  COMMIT: friend-tla-delivery-states: Friend.tla models batch delivery, answered pings, the silent stop, broken sessions and one-shot lanes
  VERDICT: MCFriend.cfg passes under TLC; each new MCFriendBroken*.cfg fails with the expected invariant; RUNS.tsv carries a row per run; counterexamples checked against the code.

STEP 3. Run TLC on hetzner for every cfg you touched and record the last lines; then `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci` (the tree's model checks) and record its last line. Commit only PATHS.

STEP 4. END. Push normally with `git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/<the STATUS line's branch>`; never force. Verify `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<that branch>` equals `git rev-parse HEAD`. Write `~/zhi-working/outbox/<job>/REPORT.md` beginning `Verdict: LAND` and `Head: <full 40-hex remote tip>`, followed by one paragraph stating the model change, the TLC results and any findings in the code. Use HOLD or FAIL with the precise blocker when no truthful LAND is possible. Write RESULT.md beside it carrying this card's RESULT line. Create no pull request.

DONE-WHEN: MCFriend.cfg passes and every reversed witness fails under TLC on hetzner, with RUNS rows committed.

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.")
