THE TASK. The Claude Code route into the open session, measured, and the hand watch script retired. Glenn, 2026-10-04 1:02 PM ET: friends keep running in their own harness (the desktop apps). Reliable comms means the daemon reaches the OPEN session in that harness, never a separate headless thread. And 12:55 PM: \"users of nova-tools will not want to have to launch harnesses in special ways\": no route may need a special launch of the harness (a flag, an environment variable or a wrapper at app start). A session doing something once inside itself (running a command the install prints) is allowed and is said in the help.

Claude Code has no command that puts a turn into a running session from outside; what it has is a background task whose exit re-invokes the session. So the route is the session's own blocking read: the session keeps `nova-bus wait --as <me> --after <cursor> --wake-file <file>` (landed by fg-bus-wait-verb) running as a background task, re-armed with the cursor it printed each time it returns; the daemon is passive for claude (it takes nothing off the stream, answers the coordinator's PING with a daemon-pong, writes presence route=passive, and appends one line per message to the wake file so a wait that missed nothing still returns). Make it plain: `nova-friend install --harness claude` prints the one line the session runs and SPEC-FRIEND's Claude paragraph says the pattern. The hand script /Volumes/nova/ai/rowan/working/tmp/buswatch/watch.sh is the reference; once this lands, the coordinator's session runs the verb instead (adoption is fg-adopt-friend-daemons).

MEASURED ACCEPTANCE, on the Studio, the friend's real open session: ten times, a real bus message to the friend (`nova-bus send --as rowan --to <friend> --subject 'reply: <nonce>' --body 'reply on the bus with subject <nonce>'`; a PING is the daemon's and is never pushed as a turn, per fg-delivery-pending-as-one-turn) is answered by the SESSION's own bus line with that subject within 60 s (`nova-bus wait --as rowan` sees it; a daemon-pong does not count), and the turn is visible in the open chat window, in the same session id, during that minute (the harness's own transcript of that session shows the turn: name the file and the line). Record each run: sent at, turn seen at, pong at, seconds. Ten of ten within 60 s is LAND; anything less is HOLD with the runs. Where no route exists, the card's end is the proof (what was tried, the exact refusal or silence measured) plus the fallback below, and the daemon reports route=defer or passive in presence, never a silent loss.
GENERAL: what this card adds imports no internal/sprint*, internal/nsprint* or internal/sprintwire package, says no sprint word in help or docs, and waits on no sprint server.
Unit tests use no real time and open no socket: an injected clock (or testing/synctest) and the package's fake store; the logic is a function apart from its transport (a server is a function of its input, a client takes a send function). Every new test opens with t.Parallel(), in testify. A test that needs Redis is functional (-tags functional) and runs only through tools/functionalrun --fresh-gocache --deadline 15m, never against a store on this machine.
Usable cold by an AI from the tool's help alone: the verb's help names every flag, every output line and JSON field, every exit code, and one example that runs as written; docs/CLI.md carries the same text; the verbhelp tests pin it.

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/rowan-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of origin/rowan/integration-2026-10-04. Export GOCACHE=~/rowan-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Read AGENTS.md and the governing spec section first; verify the defect or gap still exists at the tip before editing, and if it is already done, report HOLD with the exact evidence rather than duplicate it.

STEP 2. Do the task above, the red test first where there is code (the TEST line's name is the one to write; rename it in RESULT if the behaviour wants a better name).
  PATHS: internal/friend/adapter.go,internal/friend/adapter_test.go,cmd/nova-friend/main.go,cmd/nova-friend/main_test.go,docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md
  COMMIT: fg-claude-open-chatb: the Claude route: the session's own wait, the passive daemon, install prints the line
  VERDICT: the ten measured runs on the coordinator's own session are in the report and TestClaudeIsPassiveAndInstallPrintsTheSessionsWait is green

STEP 3. Obtain the shared Go-slot grant, then run `nice -n 19 env GOMAXPROCS=2 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/friend/ ./cmd/nova-friend ./internal/ci` and the package tests of every PATHS package, record the exact last lines, release the slot, and commit only PATHS with honest Rowan and actual model/harness attribution; `gofmt -l` on the changed files prints nothing.

STEP 4. END. Push normally with `git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/<the STATUS line's branch>`; never force. Verify `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<that branch>` equals `git rev-parse HEAD` (the full 40-hex sha, never a short one). Write `~/rowan-working/outbox/<job>/REPORT.md` beginning `Verdict: LAND` and `Head: <full 40-hex remote tip>`, followed by one paragraph stating the change, the measurements and the exact gates. Use HOLD or FAIL with the precise blocker when no truthful LAND is possible. Write RESULT.md beside it carrying this card's RESULT line. Create no pull request; the sprint consumes the branch and report.

