THE TASK. The coordinator's wake as a nova-friend verb. Glenn, 2026-10-04 1:12 PM ET: \"this stuff you are doing now should probably be formalized into nova-friend tool\". The coordinator ran this by hand today; this card makes it a verb any coordinator of friends uses, with no nova-sprint. The hand script is /Volumes/nova/ai/rowan/working/tmp/buswatch/watch.sh (read it first). `nova-bus wait` (fg-bus-wait-verb) is the bus primitive; this verb is the coordinator's use of it, with nothing to remember between runs:
- `nova-friend watch --as <coordinator> [--timeout <duration>] [--state-dir <d>] [--redis <addr>] [--json]`: waits on the coordinator's stream, the coordinator's wake file (in its state dir, where the claude adapter appends) and events (bus messages whose subject starts `event:`, sent by any tool, e.g. `event: machine stopped unasked`), skipping its own messages, ping, pong, daemon-pong and keepalive; the cursor is saved in the state dir after each run, so the next run misses nothing and needs no flag.
- Exits on the first wake with one line per wake (up to 5): `WATCH MESSAGE id=<id> from=<f> subject=<s>`, `WATCH EVENT id=<id> from=<f> subject=<s>`, `WATCH WAKE line=<text>`, then `WATCH OK after=<cursor>` exit 0; `WATCH NONE waited=<d>` exit 1 past --timeout (default forever); 2 could not run. A session that runs it in the background is re-invoked by its exit; the help says that in one sentence with the line to run.
- Built on internal/bus's wait (no second copy of its rules); the cursor file is atomic (write and rename).
