THE TASK. The escalation ladder that gets a silent friend's attention, as a verb. Glenn, 2026-10-04 1:12 PM ET: \"this stuff you are doing now should probably be formalized into nova-friend tool\". The coordinator ran this by hand today; this card makes it a verb any coordinator of friends uses, with no nova-sprint. The coordinator asked for it as `nova-friend wake <friend>`; that name is taken by the sleep pair (`nova-friend sleep`/`wake --as <me>`, a friend ending its own recorded sleep, landed by fg-friend-keepalive-into-integration), and one verb doing two things fails the one-thing rule, so this verb is `reach` (say so in the PR; if the coordinator renames it, the help's `see also` line names both).
- `nova-friend reach --as <coordinator> <friend> [--step-timeout <duration>] [--from <bus|push|window>] [--dry-run] [--json]`. The ladder, each step recorded as one line before the next starts, each waiting up to --step-timeout (default 60s) for proof, a bus line from the session (a real message, or a pong for the nonce the step carries):
  1. bus: a bus message to the friend carrying a nonce and the exact pong line (`REACH STEP step=bus sent=<id> nonce=<n>`);
  2. push: the daemon pushes the message into the session as a turn (a real message, never a PING, which is the daemon's own; the daemon must be up by presence, else the step is skipped with the reason);
  3. window: the friend's own window: a tmux-hosted TUI by send-keys into its pane (the tmux adapter's idle rule); a GUI harness through the macOS accessibility API (the harness app's window found by its bundle, the message typed into its composer and submitted), which needs the accessibility permission a person grants to the binary, refused with that remedy when absent, never asked for by the tool.
  Each step ends `REACH PROOF step=<s> after=<seconds> by=<pong|message>` and stops the ladder, or `REACH NONE step=<s> waited=<d>` and climbs. The end: `REACH OK friend=<f> step=<s>` exit 0, or `REACH FAILED friend=<f> tried=<steps>` exit 1 (say so on the bus to the coordinator's own stream, one message); exit 2 could not run.
- The ladder is a pure state machine over (step, proof seen, clock) with each side effect an injected func; tests use a fake Exec, a fake bus, a fake clock.
MEASURED: on the Studio, reach each friend once with the daemon stopped (step 3 must be the one that lands for a GUI or tmux friend) and once with it up (step 1 or 2 lands); each run's lines in the report.
GENERAL: what this card adds imports no internal/sprint*, internal/nsprint* or internal/sprintwire package, says no sprint word in help or docs, and waits on no sprint server.
Unit tests use no real time and open no socket: an injected clock (or testing/synctest) and the package's fake store; the logic is a function apart from its transport (a server is a function of its input, a client takes a send function). Every new test opens with t.Parallel(), in testify. A test that needs Redis is functional (-tags functional) and runs only through tools/functionalrun --fresh-gocache --deadline 15m, never against a store on this machine.
Usable cold by an AI from the tool's help alone: the verb's help names every flag, every output line and JSON field, every exit code, and one example that runs as written; docs/CLI.md carries the same text; the verbhelp tests pin it.
Tests: TestReachClimbsTheLadderOnlyUntilProof, TestReachSkipsThePushWhenTheDaemonIsDown, TestReachWindowRefusesWithoutAccessibilityPermission, TestReachFailedSaysSoOnceOnTheBus, TestReachDryRunPrintsTheLadder. TLA+: a small module tla/Reach.tla (states bus, push, window, ok, failed; invariants: no step after a proof, every step bounded, failed only after all three) with one Broken config; TLC on a bench machine, never the Studio. SPEC-FRIEND: a section \"Reach\". CLI.md and help: reach.

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/rowan-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of origin/rowan/integration-2026-10-04. Export GOCACHE=~/rowan-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Read AGENTS.md and the governing spec section first; verify the defect or gap still exists at the tip before editing, and if it is already done, report HOLD with the exact evidence rather than duplicate it.

STEP 2. Do the task above, the red test first where there is code (the TEST line's name is the one to write; rename it in RESULT if the behaviour wants a better name).
  PATHS: internal/friend/**,cmd/nova-friend/main.go,cmd/nova-friend/main_test.go,cmd/nova-friend/verbhelp_test.go,docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md,docs/CLI.md,tla/README.md,tla/RUNS.tsv,tla/CASES.tsv,cmd/nova-friend/reach.go,cmd/nova-friend/reach_test.go,internal/friend/window_darwin.go,internal/friend/window_other.go,internal/friend/window_test.go,tla/Reach.tla,tla/MCReach.tla,tla/MCReach.cfg,tla/MCReachBrokenStepAfterProof.cfg
