Deadline: finish within 30 minutes.

You are a child of the coordinator: one task, one checkout, one branch, unattended; this card is the whole task. You start in the job directory (export JOB=$PWD): read $JOB/JOB.md first, work in the staged checkout it names (a full clone at BASE), commit as usual and finish as it says. No gh, no push: JOB.md's finish does both.
Libraries considered: testify (require for setup, assert in rows), the tree's internal/testkit (Main/Ran, Refusals, Tree, WriteFile, ReadFile, JSON, Waits; read internal/testkit/HARNESS.md) and testing/synctest for virtual time; nothing third-party is added, and a rig stays a small struct in the package's own test files.
The contract is docs/STANDARD.md (embedded in AGENTS.md): read the sections a step names first; where this card and it disagree, it wins and the PR body says so.
Steps marked (hard) were dealt pro in the flat wave and may need pro; the card is dealt flash first and the machine escalates, never you.

THE TASK. A tree of 1 work step (STEP 2 to STEP 2), walked in order. Each work step carries its own PATHS:, COMMIT: and VERDICT: lines: do it, run its check, commit only its PATHS with its COMMIT: line as the message, and write its verdict line in the PR body and RESULT, `step <n>: <ok|broken|not-done|skipped> <the full 40-hex commit sha pasted from git rev-parse HEAD, or - when nothing changed; a short sha is refused: e.g. step 2: ok 3b1f0c2a9d4e7f6a5c8b1d0e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f90 the change> <one line>` (ok with `-` and the commit that did it when the head already holds the step). The first step that is not ok stops the walk: steps before it land, and the coordinator turns the rest into a new card. No singletons; every test parallel (docs/STANDARD.md section 8: \"Every test opens with `t.Parallel()` ..., so the environment and working directory are injected through the code's config, never set with `t.Setenv` or a Chdir\"; the owner: \"Tests should always have their own instances of all relevant objects. no globals.\"). For each test the step names that internal/ci/testdata/serial-tests_allowlist.txt lists (its reason says which: `t.Setenv`, `t.Chdir`, `swaps package var <name>`), find what the code reads (`os.Getenv`, `os.Getwd`, `os.UserHomeDir`, a package variable a test swaps) and pass it in: a `getenv func(string) string`, a working directory, a home path, or a field of the instance the test builds (as cmd/nova-sprint's `newApp` takes `getenv`); main passes the real ones. The test sets its own instance's value and opens with `t.Parallel()`; its ledger row goes and the package's `env` row in internal/ci/testdata/testify/ falls (the gate's update). A test that cannot be made parallel without a change outside PATHS keeps its row and is named with the change it needs.

HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED. (1) Every behaviour a test pinned before is pinned after: count the checks (assert and require calls, table rows) before and after, and break three of the behaviours in the code on purpose to see the tests go red, then restore. (2) Production code changes only where a step says, and never its output. (3) No sleep, timer wait, socket, real clock or `t.Setenv` is added to a unit test; every test touched opens with `t.Parallel()`. (4) Test names are kept unless a step says otherwise (a Test that becomes a table row keeps its name as the row's). (5) Nothing outside PATHS and NEW. (6) The production path reads the same environment as before: main passes the real ones.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names (cd <that path>) and run git log --oneline -1: the head is 36f4c5ba6371 or a later commit of BASE. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/gocache GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Sites and counts here were read at 36f4c5ba6371: find a moved line by its text.
STEP 2. (hard) tests of internal/ci run in parallel.
  PATHS: internal/ci/testify_shapes_test.go, internal/ci/*.go, internal/ci/testdata/serial-tests_allowlist.txt, internal/ci/testdata/testify/internal/ci.txt
