      :brief "REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: fix-red
CLASS: model
LEG: go
DEADLINE: finish within 150 minutes
DEPENDS-ON: setup-nova-doctor
PATHS: internal/doctor/check_tailnet.go,internal/doctor/check_tailnet_test.go,docs/SETUP.md,internal/up/tailnet*.go
SHARED: docs/SETUP.md
TEST: ./internal/doctor TestDoctorTailnetCheckNamesTheMissingPeer
Deadline: finish within 150 minutes.
Libraries considered: the tree's own packages and testify; no new dependency.

ATTRIBUTION. Commits and reports name the friend (By: rowan-next) and your actual model and harness. Never claim a model or harness you are not running. A Claude worker writes the true Claude trailer.

THE TASK. nova-tools v1.2.0, lens setup (Glenn 2026-10-04: a stranger sets the whole thing up from the docs and the tools, with nothing hidden; nothing the coordinator needs is a Rowan-only tool). One card per hidden dependency: this one is the tailnet: the fleet's machines reach each other and the stores only over it (the tools refuse non-loopback, non-tailnet addresses). Read cmd/nova-config/machine.go and internal/config/self.go for how a machine's tailnet name is known. The check: tailscale is installed and up, this machine has its name, and each machine of the nova-config inventory answers by name; under --local it is skipped with the reason (card sprint-local-only-mode makes local-only a mode of nova-sprint). Ship it where nova-up can (in internal/up/tailnet*.go, a step of nova-up: --local where it applies to one machine, else the fleet mode), else document it; either way add the doctor check internal/doctor/check_tailnet.go (the frame of card setup-nova-doctor: one file, self-registering) with the fix line, and a section in docs/SETUP.md headed with this card id (what the dependency is, who needs it, how nova-up provides it or how a person does, what the doctor checks). The worker never runs nova-up or a doctor fix against the Studio, a bench's real services or any fleet store: tests use fakes behind interfaces (a fake exec, a fake filesystem rooted in t.TempDir(), an injected clock), and no test starts a service or opens a socket to a shared one. The red test first: the check on a fake Env, failing while the dependency is missing or wrong and passing when it is right, each fix line naming a real verb or the documented step. Edit only the files PATHS names; a change that needs another file is a HOLD naming it. Other cards of this batch also edit docs/SETUP.md (the SHARED line): add your paragraph as its own subsection headed with this card id, under the section it belongs to, and change no other paragraph of it.

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/rowan-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of origin/rowan/integration-2026-10-04. Export GOCACHE=~/rowan-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Read AGENTS.md and the docs named in PATHS first.

STEP 2. Do the task above, writing the red test first on the twin store or with fakes; no test opens a real socket to a shared service or sleeps on the wall clock.
  PATHS: internal/doctor/check_tailnet.go,internal/doctor/check_tailnet_test.go,docs/SETUP.md,internal/up/tailnet*.go
  COMMIT: dep-tailnet: setup: the tailnet, as a doctor check and a documented requirement
  VERDICT: nova-doctor checks the tailnet (tailscale present, logged in, each inventory machine reachable by its tailnet name) and, under --local, skips it saying why.

STEP 3. Run on a Linux bench (vision or hetzner), never on the Studio: `nice -n 10 env GOMAXPROCS=4 go test -p 2 ./internal/doctor -run 'TestDoctorTailnetCheckNamesTheMissingPeer' -count=1 -timeout 600s`, then `nice -n 10 env GOMAXPROCS=4 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/doctor ./internal/up`, record exact last lines, and commit only PATHS with honest attribution; `gofmt -l` on the changed files prints nothing.

STEP 4. END. Push normally with `git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/<the STATUS line's branch>`; never force. Verify `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<that branch>` equals `git rev-parse HEAD`. Write `~/rowan-working/outbox/<job>/REPORT.md` beginning `Verdict: LAND` and `Head: <full 40-hex remote tip>`, followed by one paragraph stating the change and exact gates. Use HOLD or FAIL with the precise blocker when no truthful LAND is possible. Write RESULT.md beside it carrying this card's RESULT line. Create no pull request; the sprint consumes the branch and report.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/doctor -run TestDoctorTailnetCheckNamesTheMissingPeer` passes at the head.

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.")
