    (:stream "classes" :cards
     ((:id "classes-spec-ci-10-t" :tier "-" :needs ("classes-wave3b" "classes-spec-ci-9-t")
      :title "A tree of 1 work step (STEP 2 to STEP 2), walked in order"
      :brief "RESULT: classes-spec-ci-10-t sha=36f4c5ba6371 tier: flash
REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: sweep
CLASS: model
DEPENDS-ON: classes-wave3b,classes-spec-ci-9-t
PATHS: docs/SPEC-CI.md, docs/STANDARD.md, AGENTS.md
NEW: internal/ci/**
TEST: internal/docs TestCommittedMapMatchesTree
Deadline: finish within 30 minutes.

You are a child of the coordinator: one task, one checkout, one branch, unattended; this card is the whole task. You start in the job directory (export JOB=$PWD): read $JOB/JOB.md first, work in the staged checkout it names (a full clone at BASE), commit as usual and finish as it says. No gh, no push: JOB.md's finish does both.
Libraries considered: the tree's internal/ci/allowlist (the one shrink-only ledger reader and writer), go/ast and go/parser for a source scan, os/exec with a deadline for a run of a built tool, testify; nothing third-party is added.
NEW names the files this card creates; they and PATHS are this card's files, no others.
The contract is docs/STANDARD.md (embedded in AGENTS.md): read the sections a step names first; where this card and it disagree, it wins and the PR body says so.
Steps marked (hard) were dealt pro in the flat wave and may need pro; the card is dealt flash first and the machine escalates, never you.

THE TASK. A tree of 1 work step (STEP 2 to STEP 2), walked in order. Each work step carries its own PATHS:, COMMIT: and VERDICT: lines: do it, run its check, commit only its PATHS with its COMMIT: line as the message, and write its verdict line in the PR body and RESULT, `step <n>: <ok|broken|not-done|skipped> <the full 40-hex commit sha pasted from git rev-parse HEAD, or - when nothing changed; a short sha is refused: e.g. step 2: ok 3b1f0c2a9d4e7f6a5c8b1d0e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f90 the change> <one line>` (ok with `-` and the commit that did it when the head already holds the step). The first step that is not ok stops the walk: steps before it land, and the coordinator turns the rest into a new card. Each rule names its class test (docs/STANDARD.md section 10). A class test is built like the tree's other counted class tests (internal/ci/allowlist: a shrink-only ledger, one shard per tool or package, `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1` lowers only), seeded with what the head holds (the seeding run is the one time rows are written: say so), with a witness: a fixture that breaks the rule once is refused naming the site, and the fixed fixture passes. Its entry goes in docs/SPEC-CI.md under The class tests (the rule, the mistake it prevents, its ledger, its remedy line), its name where docs/STANDARD.md states the rule, and `make map` regenerates the class-rules list.

HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED. (1) Each step's change is the one the step names and no other: every +/- line of `git diff -U0` traces to one sentence of its step. (2) Behaviour no step names is unchanged: the package's existing tests pass unedited, except an expected line a step itself changes. (3) A new behaviour has a test that fails before the change and passes after (write it first, see it red), named for what it pins, opening with `t.Parallel()`, in testify. (4) A printed event prefix or field name that docs/TESTS.md shows is kept: add a field, never rename one, unless the step says so. (5) A refusal names what the input wants and the command to run next, in the skeleton's grammar (`VERB REFUSED: <why>; run: <remedy>`). (6) Nothing is guessed: where the code cannot tell what is right, the PR body says so and the step ends partial.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names (cd <that path>) and run git log --oneline -1: the head is 36f4c5ba6371 or a later commit of BASE. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/gocache GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Sites and counts here were read at 36f4c5ba6371: find a moved line by its text.
STEP 2. (hard) class test help-cites.
  PATHS: docs/SPEC-CI.md, docs/STANDARD.md, AGENTS.md, internal/ci/**
  COMMIT: classes-spec-ci-10-t: class test help-cites
  VERDICT: ok when read docs/SPEC-CI.md's entry for one counted class test (`deadcode` or `testify`) and its code, and internal/ci/allowlist. Write the witness first, then the scan, then seed the ledger at the head (the seeding run is the one time rows are written: say so in the PR body), then the docs and `make map`; not-done or broken naming what remains
Add the class test `help-cites` (docs/STANDARD.md sections 2 and 4; raters found \"practice 17\" and SPEC rule numbers in help). It scans every tool's `help`, `help <verb>` and topic output and refuses a reference the reader cannot follow from the binary: a source path under cmd/ or internal/, an issue or PR number (`#1234`), a spec rule number (`rule 7`, `§5`), a person's or machine's name. Build it like the tree's other counted class tests (internal/ci/allowlist: a shrink-only ledger, one shard per tool or package under internal/ci/testdata/help-cites/, `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1` lowers only), seeded with what the head holds today, so it lands green and every port or fix card lowers its own row. It has a witness test: a fixture that breaks the rule once is refused naming the site, and the fixed fixture passes. Add its entry to docs/SPEC-CI.md under The class tests (the rule, the mistake it prevents, its ledger, its remedy line), put its name in docs/STANDARD.md where the rule it holds is stated (\"Check: ...\"), and run `make map` so the class-rules list in docs/STANDARD.md section 12 and AGENTS.md carry it. A functional walk runs under `//go:build functional` and through `tools/functionalrun` only, never against a store.
STEP 3. Read `git diff -U0` from the start commit against HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED, hunk by hunk; fix in the step that owns the hunk.
STEP 4. Run the gate once, each line as written, keeping each last line: `nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ ./internal/docs/`. If a test in ./internal/ci/ fails naming a ledger row (\"delete the stale entry\", \"below allowed count\", \"shrink the count\", \"lower the row\"), run `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1 nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '<the failing tests, joined with |>'`, then the gate again. Keep only the ledger lines of files PATHS names and the shards internal/ci/testdata/<ledger>/<package>.txt of its packages; restore any other it rewrote; name a needed one (partial). A row only shrinks. Not yours: TestGeneralityText red on two stale SPEC-BUS-DELIVERY.md rows (dead-generality-text-t2 deletes them).
