THE TASK. ReadBox decodes with json.Unmarshal into a *Box (internal/fuse/fuse.go:203-215, type Box :99-102): unknown keys are ignored, key matching is case-insensitive and a duplicated key is last-wins, and a whole-box JSON null leaves the zero Box. Trigger: a box whose only lockdown object sits under a misspelled key (lockdwn) verifies clear (check exit 0); a box with two lockdown keys whose later value is null verifies clear; a box that is just null verifies clear (the null refusal commit 1750ad8af is on the sprint branch and is not in dev). The correct single key blows. Impact: a typo or a hand edit silently opens the gate on a box meant to be blown. Remedy: read with a json.Decoder with DisallowUnknownFields, and walk the raw tokens of the top-level object first (json.Decoder.Token) to refuse a duplicate key and anything that is not an object (null, array, string); refuse trailing data after the value. Do not require both keys to be present (hand-edited sparse boxes such as {\"quarantine\":{...}} are normal and TestNullQuarantineStillYieldsAUsableMap at fuse_test.go:126 keeps a null quarantine readable). Test: ReadBox errors for {\"lockdwn\":{\"at\":\"t\",\"reason\":\"r\"},\"quarantine\":{}}, for {\"lockdown\":{\"at\":\"t\",\"reason\":\"r\"},\"quarantine\":{},\"lockdown\":null}, for null, and for a valid box followed by garbage; a single correct key still blows (Lockdown non-nil); red before, green after. (security#74 finding 8, persists from security#55) The work lives in the files of the PATHS line, and those are the only files you may touch; a change any other file needs goes in the report as a proposed diff, never a commit. The test named on the TEST line is red before the change and green after.

