THE TASK. The member-prefix and epoch-key reservations miss the view family (security#78 finding 5). At dev internal/nsprint/fn/lua/table.lua T.shape (about lines 469-475) reserves for epoch_key the key 'tables' and every 'table:' key, and for member_prefix every 'table:' prefix other than 'table::member:', but not the view family that ns_view_set/state/del own (key 'view:<name>' hashes at about line 1646-1690, and the 'views' SET). Triggers, all accepted at create: 'nova-table create t --columns done --member-prefix view:' (member records land on stored-view hashes and interleave fields), '--epoch-key views' (every verb of that table then fails WRONGTYPE once a view exists), '--epoch-key view:today' (a view hash field is silently read as the epoch). Remedy: in the T.shape CONFIG check refuse epoch_key == 'views' or a prefix 'view:' and member_prefix with prefix 'view:' (also a member_prefix equal to 'view:' family such as 'view:x:'); the bind check in T.rowfields (about line 850) can still name view:* keys, so either reserve them too or state in docs/SPEC-NOVA-TABLE.md that binds may name an external view-family set. Also check the Go side if it validates the same config (internal/ntable/ntable.go MemberPrefix/EpochKey). Test (functional tier): create with each of the three flags above and assert the CONFIG refusal and that no definition was written; a plain prefix like 'job:member:' still creates. Red before, green after. The work lives in the files of the PATHS line, and those are the only files you may touch; a change any other file needs goes in the report as a proposed diff, never a commit. The test named on the TEST line is red before the change and green after.

