      (:id "sec-gate-names-the-check-not-the-rule" :tier "-" :needs ("sec-gate-marks-verb-made-files")
      :title "Model: tla/SecretsSeat.tla on sprint/md-secrets-h.w1.g1.e15; cite it from the code change"
      :brief "RESULT: sec-gate-names-the-check-not-the-rule sha=2d720d219ff5 tier: flash
REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: fix-red
CLASS: model
LEG: go
DEADLINE: finish within 45 minutes
DEPENDS-ON: sec-gate-marks-verb-made-files
PATHS: internal/secrets/**,docs/SPEC-SECRETS.md
TEST: ./internal/secrets TestGateRefusalNamesTheCheck
Deadline: finish within 45 minutes.
Libraries considered: Go standard library and testify, already in tree; no new dependency. v1.2.0 security, fix-as-found; a one-line code change and a doc change, with a failing test first. Chained after sec-gate-marks-verb-made-files because both edit gate.go and the spec's gate section; start from the BASE tip that holds it (the gate may then have one more check; number it too).

ATTRIBUTION. Commits may use the machine's git identity for now, but every commit body carries a line `By: <who did the work>` above the Co-Authored-By trailer: the friend's name for a friend card (By: Rowan), the route's model name for a fleet child (e.g. By: deepseek-v4.1-flash). Commits end with the trailer Co-Authored-By: Claude <model> <noreply@anthropic.com> as nova-tools AGENTS.md and docs/STANDARD.md require, naming the actual model; the report names the model and the harness.

THE TASK. Model: tla/SecretsSeat.tla on sprint/md-secrets-h.w1.g1.e15; cite it from the code change. The model (LAND b386b2d1, TLC green) found, while its counterexamples were checked by hand against the gate's output: the gate's refusal line `GATE REFUSE rule=<n> file=<f>: <why>` (internal/secrets/gate.go, gateRefuse, line 259-262 at BASE) prints as `rule=` the POSITION of the matching creation rule in `.sops.yaml` (1-based; 0 for a file no rule names), never WHICH CHECK refused. The spec's gate section lists the checks in prose (a changed rule's two recipients and one seat file; a changed seat file encrypted with its rule present; no other file; a seat gone at head; the registry) and the card briefs and the model name them \"check 1..4\", but a reader of a refusal cannot tell check 2 from check 4 by the line, and `rule=1` reads as \"rule 1 of the spec\" to anyone who has not read gate.go. Fix: the refusal names the check. Keep `rule=<n>` exactly as it is (tests and the store's workflow read it) and add one field, `check=<k>`, between `rule=` and `file=`: `GATE REFUSE rule=<n> check=<k> file=<f>: <why>`, where k is the check's number in a numbered list the spec's gate section gains (1 the rule's recipients and path_regex, 2 the seat file's encryption and its rule, 3 no other file changes, 4 a new recipient needs the registry's seat, 5 a seat gone at head, in the order gate.go runs them; renumber to match gate.go's real order if it differs, and say so). gateRefuse takes the check number; every call site passes its own; the spec's gate section carries the numbered list and the grammar line with `check=`.
The failing test first, in internal/secrets: TestGateRefusalNamesTheCheck runs RunGate on a store whose head adds a seat file in the clear (check 2) and on one whose head adds a stray file (check 3), and asserts each line carries `check=2` and `check=3` respectively and still carries the same `rule=` it does today. It is red at BASE because no line carries `check=`. Existing tests that assert the whole line (gate_rules_test.go, gate_broken_regex_test.go and the others that `assert.Equal` a full `GATE REFUSE` line) are updated to the new line in the same commit; tests that `Contains` `rule=1` need no change.

STEP 1. Enter the staged checkout JOB.md names, no clone; inspect git status and the actual full head. Work only on its own branch. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any Go command. Scratch belongs under $JOB/scratch. Read AGENTS.md and the `gate` section of docs/SPEC-SECRETS.md first; cite the spec and the model (tla/SecretsSeat.tla on sprint/md-secrets-h.w1.g1.e15) from gateRefuse. Verify the defect still exists before editing: no `check=` in any gate line at BASE; if already fixed, report not-done with the exact evidence rather than duplicate work.

STEP 2. Make it red first: write TestGateRefusalNamesTheCheck, run `nice -n 19 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/secrets -run '^TestGateRefusalNamesTheCheck$'`, and keep the failing line as evidence. Then make it green by changing only the named PATHS, minimally. Commit the draft on your own branch as soon as the test is green, before any further probe. A change any other file needs (cmd/nova-secrets help text that prints the grammar line, the store's workflow) goes in the report as a proposed diff, never a commit.
  PATHS: internal/secrets/**,docs/SPEC-SECRETS.md
  COMMIT: sec-gate-names-the-check-not-the-rule: a gate refusal names its check (check=<k>) beside the rule position (SPEC-SECRETS gate)
  VERDICT: every GATE REFUSE line carries check=<k>; rule=<n> is unchanged; the spec's gate section numbers the checks in gate.go's order and shows the grammar; the model is cited from gateRefuse.

STEP 3. Run the gate: `nice -n 19 go test -count=1 -race -timeout 600s ./internal/secrets/ ./cmd/nova-secrets/` and keep the last line of each. Run `gofmt -l` on every changed Go file; it must print nothing. No Redis or external service is needed.

STEP 4. Inspect the diff and commit only the named PATHS on your own branch, with the `By:` line and the trailer above. Present-tense comments and docs; no names of people, machines or friends. Finish exactly through JOB.md's protocol, no direct external publication; the SHA in RESULT.md is the exact 40-hex `git rev-parse HEAD`. Report the actual gates, the red-to-green evidence, the diff stat, and what was not done. Normal independent review is required before landing; never merge yourself.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/secrets -run TestGateRefusalNamesTheCheck` passes at the head.

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.")
