      (:id "sec-gate-marks-verb-made-files" :tier "-" :needs ("sec-seat-add-refuses-foreign-pub")
      :title "Model: tla/SecretsSeat.tla on sprint/md-secrets-h.w1.g1.e15; cite it from the code change"
      :brief "RESULT: sec-gate-marks-verb-made-files sha=2d720d219ff5 tier: pro
REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: fix-red
CLASS: model
LEG: go
DEADLINE: finish within 120 minutes
DEPENDS-ON: sec-seat-add-refuses-foreign-pub
PATHS: internal/secrets/**,cmd/nova-secrets/**,docs/SPEC-SECRETS.md
TEST: ./internal/secrets TestGateTellsAVerbMadeSealFromAHandSeal
Deadline: finish within 120 minutes.
Libraries considered: Go standard library and testify, already in tree; no new dependency. v1.2.0 security, fix-as-found: a defect the model found is fixed the same hour with a failing test first. Chained after sec-seat-add-refuses-foreign-pub because both edit internal/secrets, cmd/nova-secrets and the spec; start from the BASE tip that holds it.

ATTRIBUTION. Commits may use the machine's git identity for now, but every commit body carries a line `By: <who did the work>` above the Co-Authored-By trailer: the friend's name for a friend card (By: Rowan), the route's model name for a fleet child (e.g. By: deepseek-v4.1-flash). Commits end with the trailer Co-Authored-By: Claude <model> <noreply@anthropic.com> as nova-tools AGENTS.md and docs/STANDARD.md require, naming the actual model; the report names the model and the harness.

THE TASK. Model: tla/SecretsSeat.tla on sprint/md-secrets-h.w1.g1.e15; cite it from the code change. The model (LAND b386b2d1, TLC green; the MCSecretsSeatReachHandSeal config) found, and a hand check of the counterexample confirmed: a seat file sealed BY HAND (`sops <seat>.yaml`, `sops updatekeys <seat>.yaml`, or any editor that leaves sops metadata and ENC[ values) is indistinguishable, to the gate, from a file a verb wrote. Gate check 2 (internal/secrets/gate.go around lines 181-201 at BASE: sops metadata present, no plain `KEY: value` outside unencrypted_regex, a rule exists) is a check on the BYTES, and a hand seal produces the same bytes. So every guarantee the verbs add on top of sops (seat add's re-seal only out of a seat the operator can open, seal's decrypt-before-write, the `--only` names, the receipts) is bypassed by a hand seal the gate approves. And the spec's own first-run section (\"The first run: six lines a stranger pastes\", docs/SPEC-SECRETS.md) tells people to do exactly that: \"a holder of an existing key seals the file in a second PR — `sops rowan.yaml` if it is new, `sops updatekeys rowan.yaml` if it exists\". The spec recommends the path the model shows the gate cannot see. This card DECIDES, in the card, whether the gate should mark verb-made files, and fixes the spec either way:
  (yes) A verb that writes a seat file leaves a mark the gate can read and a hand seal does not leave by accident: the simplest truthful mark is a sops-metadata-adjacent comment line or an unencrypted key permitted by the rule's unencrypted_regex, e.g. a root key `NOVA_SECRETS_WRITTEN_BY: seat add|seal <tool version>` that the rule's unencrypted_regex permits in the clear (the spec already permits such keys), written by `seal` and `seat add` on every write and checked by the gate as a new check: a changed seat file without the mark is `GATE REFUSE ... : the seat file was not written by a nova-secrets verb; seal it with nova-secrets seal or seat add, never by hand`. A mark is not a signature (a hand can copy it), so the spec says plainly what it catches (a hand seal by accident, the first-run instructions, a stranger who did not read the spec) and what it does not (a hand that forges the mark; that is the registry's and the reviewer's business). The first-run section then tells a stranger to ask a holder to run `nova-secrets seat add`, never `sops`.
  (no) The gate stays a check on bytes, the spec's gate section says in one paragraph that a hand seal is approved and why that is acceptable (what else stands: check 1 on the rule, check 4 with the registry, the reviewer), and the first-run section is rewritten so that the recommended path is `nova-secrets seat add` by a holder of an existing key, with the hand `sops` lines kept only as the recovery path and labelled as the path the gate cannot tell apart.
Choose by the model's invariant (a seat file is written only by a key that opens it, or by seat add out of a seat the operator CAN open): if the gate is where that invariant is enforced for the store repo, take (yes). SAY WHICH in the report and in the spec.
The failing test first, in internal/secrets: TestGateTellsAVerbMadeSealFromAHandSeal builds a store at --base with a rule, writes `<seat>.yaml` at --head once through the tree's seal path (the fake sops that refuses what real sops refuses, with the mark) and once as a hand seal (the same bytes without the mark), runs RunGate on each diff, and asserts the verb-made file approves and the hand-made file refuses with the line above. Under (no) the test is renamed to what the spec then promises (both approve, and the spec says so) and the report says so. It is red at BASE because today both approve.

STEP 1. Enter the staged checkout JOB.md names, no clone; inspect git status and the actual full head. Work only on its own branch. Export GOCACHE=$JOB/cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any Go command. Scratch belongs under $JOB/scratch. Read AGENTS.md, docs/SPEC-SECRETS.md (`gate`, `seal`, `seat add`, \"The first run\") and internal/secrets/gate.go, seal.go and seat.go first; cite the spec and the model (tla/SecretsSeat.tla on sprint/md-secrets-h.w1.g1.e15) from every function the change touches. Verify the defect still exists before editing: at BASE the gate approves a hand-sealed file and the first-run section says `sops rowan.yaml`; if already fixed, report not-done with the exact evidence rather than duplicate work.

STEP 2. Make it red first: write TestGateTellsAVerbMadeSealFromAHandSeal, run `nice -n 19 go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/secrets -run '^TestGateTellsAVerbMadeSealFromAHandSeal$'`, and keep the failing line as evidence. Then make it green by changing only the named PATHS, minimally. Commit the draft on your own branch as soon as the test is green, before any further probe; a later commit may refine it. A change any other file needs goes in the report as a proposed diff, never a commit. The store repo's own workflow (`.github/seat-rule-gate.sh` in mas-bandwidth/secrets) is NOT in PATHS: if the yes-path needs it changed, the report carries the proposed diff.
  PATHS: internal/secrets/**,cmd/nova-secrets/**,docs/SPEC-SECRETS.md
  COMMIT: sec-gate-marks-verb-made-files: the gate tells a verb-made seal from a hand seal, and the first run says seat add, never sops by hand (SPEC-SECRETS gate)
  VERDICT: the decision (yes or no) is in the spec's gate section with its reason; under yes a hand-sealed seat file is refused by the gate and a verb-made one approves; the first-run section no longer tells a stranger to seal by hand; the model is cited from the change.

STEP 3. Run the gate: `nice -n 19 go test -count=1 -race -timeout 600s ./internal/secrets/ ./cmd/nova-secrets/` and keep the last line of each. Run `gofmt -l` on every changed Go file; it must print nothing. No Redis or external service is needed; a test that needs the real sops and age is skipped without them and said so in the report.

STEP 4. Inspect the diff and commit only the named PATHS on your own branch, with the `By:` line and the trailer above. Present-tense comments and docs; no names of people, machines or friends. Finish exactly through JOB.md's protocol, no direct external publication; the SHA in RESULT.md is the exact 40-hex `git rev-parse HEAD`. Report the decision and why, the actual gates, the red-to-green evidence, the diff stat, and what was not done. Normal independent review is required before landing; never merge yourself.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/secrets -run TestGateTellsAVerbMadeSealFromAHandSeal` passes at the head, and the first-run section of docs/SPEC-SECRETS.md no longer recommends a hand `sops` seal.

