     ((:id "tla-secrets" :tier "-" :needs ("tla-rel1" "tla-cairn" "seams-pkg-secrets-t" "modeltests-pkg-secrets-t")
      :title "The TLA+ model of `internal/secrets`, beside the module that owns the state (the owner, 2026-09-27: TLA+ for every state machine, in every project; 2026-10-02: models for bus, update, cairn, secrets, config, \"in order, after the existing wo"
      :brief "RESULT: tla-secrets sha=fa4c0cd3066e tier: flash
REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: sweep
CLASS: model
DEPENDS-ON: tla-rel1,tla-cairn,seams-pkg-secrets-t,modeltests-pkg-secrets-t
PATHS: tla/CASES.tsv, tla/RUNS.tsv, tla/README.md
NEW: tla/SecretsSeat.tla, tla/MCSecretsSeat.tla, tla/MCSecretsSeat*.cfg
TEST: internal/ci TestTLCRecordsCoverCurrentModels
Deadline: finish within 90 minutes.

You are a child of the coordinator: one task, one checkout, one branch, unattended; this card is the whole task. You start in the job directory (export JOB=$PWD): read $JOB/JOB.md first, work in the staged checkout it names (a full clone at BASE), commit as usual and finish as it says. No gh, no push: JOB.md's finish does both.
Libraries considered: the TLA+ standard modules the jar bundles (Naturals, Sequences, FiniteSets, TLC) for the module; tools/tlacheck and internal/tlc, in the tree, for the run and the records; no Go helper is written.
The contract is docs/STANDARD.md (embedded in AGENTS.md): read its section 5 (correct: a model where there is a machine) before the first edit; where this card and it disagree, it wins and the PR body says so.
A step marked (hard: <reason>) likely needs pro; the card is dealt flash first and the machine escalates, never you.

THE TASK. The TLA+ model of `internal/secrets`, beside the module that owns the state (the owner, 2026-09-27: TLA+ for every state machine, in every project; 2026-10-02: models for bus, update, cairn, secrets, config, \"in order, after the existing work, where we can (check dependencies)\"): place and its receipts, and the digest race: two places of one value at once, the store's HEAD moving between the read and the receipt. Read ValueNeverInTheClearAtRest, SeatFileNeverReplaced, OnlyRecipientsOpen, PrivateKeyStaysHome, ReceiptNamesCommittedBlob and GateRefusesEveryRuleBreak against the seams' runner, and add the concurrent place. The models stream's md card writes the module (its files are on NEW because that card is still open as this one is cut, and it lands before this card runs): bring it to the code as it now stands, after the 1.1.0 wave's seams and modeltests cards. If `tla/SecretsSeat.tla` is absent at your head, write it whole to the same rules. The module's VARIABLES are the state the Go module owns, read from the code before a line of TLA+ is written; ACTIONS are its operations and the outside events; INVARIANTS and liveness come from the rules its doc comments and spec state, each cited to its sentence; a reversed witness is one `Broken` constant in the instance and one cfg per broken case whose `expected` is `invariant` with the property it must fail, beside one control cfg that passes. An invariant the package's tests cite by name (`git grep -n -w <Name> -- internal/secrets`) keeps its name. A model that disagrees with the code is a finding, written in the PR body after it is checked by hand against the Go code, never a code change in this card. CASES.tsv rows: group `secretsseat`, gate `required`, debt `-`; the module's header comment cites the Go files and the spec section it models, present tense, no person or date; tla/README.md's table holds the module's row. Each work step carries its own PATHS:, COMMIT: and VERDICT: lines: do it, run its check, commit only its PATHS with its COMMIT: line as the message, and write its verdict line in the report, `step <n>: <ok|broken|not-done|skipped> <commit sha, or - when nothing changed> <one line>`. The first work step that is not ok stops the walk: steps before it land, and the coordinator turns the rest into a new card.

STEP 1. cd into the staged checkout JOB.md names (cd <that path>) and run git log --oneline -1: the head is fa4c0cd3066e or a later commit of BASE, and it is the head this card works on (its sha is the one a report names). Export GOCACHE=$JOB/gocache GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command.
STEP 2. (hard: a concurrent place racing the store's HEAD between the read and the receipt) the SecretsSeat model at the code.
  PATHS: tla/CASES.tsv, tla/SecretsSeat.tla, tla/MCSecretsSeat.tla, tla/MCSecretsSeat*.cfg, tla/README.md
  COMMIT: tla-secrets: the SecretsSeat model at the code
  VERDICT: ok when the module, its instance, its cfgs, its CASES.tsv rows and its README row are written and `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run TestTLCRecordsCoverCurrentModels` fails only for want of this group's records; not-done naming what remains
Read internal/secrets/ (its doc comments name the rules) and list every variable, action and invariant in the module's header comment before writing TLA+; then write or correct the module, the instance, the control cfg and at least three reversed-witness cfgs, and their CASES.tsv rows.
STEP 3. the TLC records of secretsseat.
  PATHS: tla/RUNS.tsv
  COMMIT: tla-secrets: the TLC records of secretsseat
  VERDICT: ok when tla/RUNS.tsv holds a current record for every case of the group and `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run TestTLCRecordsCoverCurrentModels` passes; skipped naming `TLC records owed: group secretsseat` on a member that is not a TLC record machine
TLC runs only on a TLC record machine (a Linux bench whose java runs and whose /opt/tla/tla2tools.jar has the SHA-256 the first word of tla/tla2tools.sha256 names), never on a working machine. Check: `uname -s` prints Linux, `command -v java`, and `shasum -a 256 /opt/tla/tla2tools.jar` equals that word. When all three hold: `go build -o $JOB/tlacheck ./tools/tlacheck`, `$JOB/tlacheck run --root . --jar /opt/tla/tla2tools.jar --dir $JOB/tlc-out --group secretsseat` (each case bounded at 110 s; a timeout is a failure, never a green), then `$JOB/tlacheck merge --root . --keep tla/RUNS.tsv --out tla/RUNS.tsv $JOB/tlc-out/RUNS.tsv`; check every counterexample TLC prints against the Go code by hand and write it in the PR body as a finding, with the code line that shows it. When any one fails: run no TLC with another jar and guess no record; leave RUNS.tsv as it is and give this step `skipped - TLC records owed: group secretsseat`. The class test is then red for this group's configs alone, the card is not landable until the records are in, and the coordinator refreshes them on this head from its seat with `tlacheck run --root . --dir <dir> --bench any` (TLC on a record machine) before the read.
