ATTRIBUTION. Commits end with the trailer Co-Authored-By: Claude <model> <noreply@anthropic.com> as nova-tools AGENTS.md and docs/STANDARD.md require, naming the actual model; reports identify Rowan and the harness. Commits may use the machine's git identity for now, but every commit body carries a line `By: <who did the work>` above the Co-Authored-By trailer: the friend's name for a friend card (By: Rowan), the route's model name for a fleet child (e.g. By: deepseek-v4.1-flash).

You are a friend of the coordinator, and this card is one sprint job (docs/FRIENDS.md), delivered as `~/rowan-working/inbox/<job>/BRIEF.md`: its STATUS line names the epoch, attempt and branch to push. Work only under `~/rowan-working/jobs/<job>/`, using `~/rowan-working/.cache/go-build`. In this card, JOB.md means the delivered BRIEF.md.

THE TASK. Design card, heavy, layer 2 of the container-sandboxed functional tier (mas-bandwidth/ideas#826, https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/ideas/issues/826). Glenn, 2026-10-04 3:09 PM: \"functional tests should probably be sandboxed (like we talked about) using say, podman.\" 3:10 PM: \"Please add podman support for functional tests to nova-sprint\". 3:11 PM: \"We have to get this stuff reliable end-to-end before we can make a 1.0.0\". Counts toward nova-tools v1.2.0, stream sandbox-v1-2-0.

What is built (do not redo it): layer 1, the image, is infra/functional-image/Containerfile with README.md and binaries.txt, held by internal/ci/functional_image_class_test.go and functional_image_runtime_class_test.go; it bakes NOVA_FUNCTIONAL_RUN=container. The runner exists as a repo tool, tools/functionalrun (`make test-functional-container`): one podman container per run, --rm --init, --network none, --ipc private, --pids-limit, --memory with no swap, a runtime-enforced `--timeout`, labels, a reaper by label and deadline, module-cache prefill with the network in a separate container. The layer-5 ansible role is built too (fleet/roles/container-runtime, fleet/container-runtime.yml: rootless podman on Linux). What is missing, and this card builds:

1. A shipped verb. `nova-ci functional` today only prints the selection (cmd/nova-ci functional.go on the sprint branch, main.go here). Add the run: `nova-ci functional --in-container [--runtime podman|docker|auto] [--deadline D] [--memory M] [--pids N] [--cpus N] [--fresh-gocache] PKG...` selects as today, then runs exactly that selection in ONE container. Move tools/functionalrun's engine (engine interface, args, reap, run) into an importable package internal/ci/functionalrun so nova-sprint can call it (card sn-functional-in-container); tools/functionalrun and `make test-functional-container` become thin callers, behaviour unchanged. The verb name and surface may be refined; the decision is written in docs/SPEC-CI.md with Glenn's words.
2. docker where present. Runtime choice: `auto` takes rootless podman first, docker second; neither present is exit 125 `CI FUNCTIONAL REFUSED reason=no_container_runtime` and the tests never run bare. docker has no `run --timeout`: state how the bound is held (an in-container timeout under --init plus the client's own deadline removal plus the reaper by the deadline label) and test the argv for both engines.
3. Every isolation flag explicit and asserted for both engines: --network none, --ipc private, --pid private, memory and memory-swap, pids, cpus, the deadline, --rm, and a forced removal at the end whatever happened; removal is the cleanup.
4. The lifecycle model. Carry PR 4708's model (draft, branch origin/rowan/functional-run-model at ef375665820f: tla/FunctionalRun.tla, MCFunctionalRun.tla/.cfg and its Broken*/Control* cfgs, future/SPEC-FUNCTIONAL-RUN.md) forward as tla/ContainerRun.tla with tla/MCContainerRun.tla and tla/MCContainerRun.cfg: variables are the container states, the client, the reaper, the clock; actions start, finish, deadline, interrupt, client killed, reap; invariants: no container outlives its deadline plus grace, the reaper never touches a foreign or young container, a cache volume is never removed; liveness: every started container is removed. Reversed witnesses tla/MCContainerRunBroken*.cfg (one per invariant, each refuted by TLC), rows in tla/CASES.tsv and tla/RUNS.tsv as internal/ci/tlc_records_class_test.go demands. TLC runs on a bench machine, never the Studio; every counterexample is checked by hand against the code before it is written down; cite the model from the code. Name PR 4708 and PR 4723 (functionalrun-src-symlink) in the PR body as superseded or folded in.

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/rowan-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of origin/rowan/integration-2026-10-04, and fetch origin/rowan/functional-run-model for the model. Export GOCACHE=~/rowan-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Read AGENTS.md, docs/SPEC-CI.md, docs/TESTING.md and infra/functional-image/README.md first; cite the spec from every function that implements a rule.

STEP 2. Do the task above, writing the red test first: the argv of both engines carries every bound and isolation flag, no runtime is a refusal and never a bare run.
  PATHS: cmd/nova-ci/**,internal/ci/functional/**,internal/ci/functionalrun/**,tools/functionalrun/**,tla/**,docs/SPEC-CI.md,docs/TESTING.md,infra/functional-image/README.md,Makefile
  COMMIT: sbx-runner-verb: nova-ci functional --in-container, podman or docker, one container per run, modelled
  VERDICT: the verb runs a selection in one container on podman and on docker with every bound; no runtime refuses; TLC green on ContainerRun and red on every Broken cfg, RUNS.tsv rows; SPEC-CI and help say it.

STEP 3. Obtain the shared Go-slot grant, then run `nice -n 19 env GOMAXPROCS=2 go test -p 2 ./cmd/nova-ci -run 'TestFunctionalInContainerHoldsTheRunInsideItsBounds' -count=1 -timeout 600s`, then `nice -n 19 env GOMAXPROCS=2 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./cmd/nova-ci ./internal/ci/... ./tools/functionalrun`, record exact last lines, release the slot, and commit only PATHS with honest Rowan and actual model/harness attribution; `gofmt -l` on the changed files prints nothing. One real run on a Linux bench with podman (`nova-ci functional --in-container ./internal/testredis`) is recorded in the report with its receipt line.

STEP 4. END. Push normally with `git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/<the STATUS line's branch>`; never force. Verify `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<that branch>` equals `git rev-parse HEAD`. Write `~/rowan-working/outbox/<job>/REPORT.md` beginning `Verdict: LAND` and `Head: <full 40-hex remote tip>`, followed by one paragraph stating the change and exact gates. Use HOLD or FAIL with the precise blocker when no truthful LAND is possible. Write RESULT.md beside it carrying this card's RESULT line. Create no pull request; the sprint consumes the branch and report.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./cmd/nova-ci -run TestFunctionalInContainerHoldsTheRunInsideItsBounds` passes at the head and TLC's RUNS.tsv rows for ContainerRun are committed.

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.")))
