     ((:id "session-recovery" :tier "-" :needs ("delivery-conformance" "message-receipts")
      :title "nova-tools v1.2.0, stream friends-v1-2-0-reliability (general, never sprint-specific)"
      :brief "REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: fix-red
CLASS: model
LEG: go
DEADLINE: finish within 180 minutes
DEPENDS-ON: delivery-conformance,message-receipts
PATHS: internal/friend/daemon*.go,internal/friend/recover*.go,internal/friend/adapter*.go,internal/friend/state*.go,cmd/nova-friend/main*.go,tla/*Friend*,tla/*.tsv,docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md
SHARED: docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md,tla/*.tsv
TEST: ./internal/friend TestBrokenSessionIsReplacedWithAHandoff
Deadline: finish within 180 minutes.
Libraries considered: the tree's own friend and bus packages (bus.Fake, the Exec seam) and testify; no new dependency.

ATTRIBUTION. Commits and reports name the friend (By: <name>) and your actual model and harness. Never claim a model or harness you are not running. A Claude worker writes the true Claude trailer.

THE TASK. nova-tools v1.2.0, stream friends-v1-2-0-reliability (general, never sprint-specific). The daemon marks a session broken after `--broken-after` identical provider refusals (internal/friend/daemon.go, `settle` and `tellBroken`) and then stays broken until a person renews the session and restarts the daemon; today (2026-10-04) one friend's broken Mercury session was fixed by hand. Make the daemon recover by itself. Broken is detected as today and also on: a context limit (the harness's context-length or prompt-too-long error), a compaction loop (the harness compacting on N turns in a row with no other output), and a turn stuck past `--stuck-after` (default 45m) with output but no tool progress. On any of them the daemon opens a fresh session in the same harness and directory (the way the one-shot lanes open one, internal/friend/lanes.go and adapter_opencode_lanes.go; each harness's open is a method on its adapter, and a harness that cannot open one says so as Deferred with the remedy), and hands it a first turn, the handoff: the friend's `inbox/QUEUE.json`, her newest cairn or status file (the newest of `cairn*.md` and `STATUS.md` in her directory, at most 32 KiB), the pong line, and every pending message. status.json carries `session=recovered from=<old id> to=<new id> reason=<...> at=<...>`, `nova-friend status` prints it, and the coordinator is told once on the bus, `friend <name>: session <old> replaced by <new>: <reason>`. At most `--recover-max` (default 3) recoveries an hour; past that the session stays broken as today and the coordinator is told it needs a person. Messages are never given up by a recovery. Extend tla/Friend.tla with broken, recovering and recovered; invariants: a recovered session got the handoff before any other turn, and recoveries are bounded; a reversed witness that TLC catches, its CASES.tsv row and RUNS.tsv run. Cite docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md; one subsection. Nothing that ships is a shell script: every loop or helper is a Go verb (Glenn, 2026-10-04 5:03 PM). Edit only the files PATHS names; a change that needs another file is a HOLD naming it. Other cards of this batch also edit docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md and tla/*.tsv (the SHARED line): add your paragraph as its own subsection headed with this card id and append rows only.

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/rowan-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of origin/rowan/integration-2026-10-04. Export GOCACHE=~/rowan-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Read AGENTS.md, docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md and tla/README.md first.

STEP 2. Do the task above, writing the red test first with bus.Fake, a fake Exec and an injected clock; no test opens a socket or sleeps on the wall clock.
  PATHS: internal/friend/daemon*.go,internal/friend/recover*.go,internal/friend/adapter*.go,internal/friend/state*.go,cmd/nova-friend/main*.go,tla/*Friend*,tla/*.tsv,docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md
  COMMIT: session-recovery: a broken, exhausted or stuck session is replaced with a handoff and reported
  VERDICT: an invalid_request streak, a context-limit error, a compaction loop and a stuck turn each open a fresh session whose first turn is the handoff; status and one bus line say so; the fourth recovery in an hour stays broken; TLC catches the reversed witness.

STEP 3. Run on a Linux bench (vision or hetzner), never on the Studio: `nice -n 10 env GOMAXPROCS=4 go test -p 2 ./internal/friend -run 'TestBrokenSessionIsReplacedWithAHandoff' -count=1 -timeout 600s`, then `nice -n 10 env GOMAXPROCS=4 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/friend ./cmd/nova-friend ./internal/ci`, then `go run ./tools/tlacheck run --dir \"$JOB/tlc\" --jar /opt/tla/tla2tools.jar` for the Friend cases; record exact last lines, and commit only PATHS with honest attribution; `gofmt -l` on the changed files prints nothing.

STEP 4. END. Push normally with `git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/<the STATUS line's branch>`; never force. Verify `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<that branch>` equals `git rev-parse HEAD`. Write `~/rowan-working/outbox/<job>/REPORT.md` beginning `Verdict: LAND` and `Head: <full 40-hex remote tip>`, followed by one paragraph stating the change and exact gates. Use HOLD or FAIL with the precise blocker when no truthful LAND is possible. Write RESULT.md beside it carrying this card's RESULT line. Create no pull request; the sprint consumes the branch and report.

DONE-WHEN: `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/friend -run TestBrokenSessionIsReplacedWithAHandoff` passes at the head.

RULES.
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Never start a server on this machine.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Report what was not done.")
      (:id "delivery-conformance" :tier "-" :needs ("session-pong" "claude-oneshot-lanesb")
      :title "nova-tools v1.2.0, stream friends-v1-2-0-reliability (general, never sprint-specific)"
      :brief "REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: fix-red
CLASS: model
LEG: go
DEADLINE: finish within 180 minutes
DEPENDS-ON: session-pong,claude-oneshot-lanes
PATHS: internal/friend/conformance*.go,cmd/nova-friend/main*.go,cmd/nova-friend/verbhelp*.go,docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md,docs/TESTING.md,docs/CLI.md
SHARED: docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md,docs/TESTING.md
TEST: ./internal/friend TestEveryAdapterPassesDeliveryConformance
Deadline: finish within 180 minutes.
Libraries considered: the tree's own friend and bus packages (bus.Fake, the adapters' Exec seam), and testify; no new dependency.

ATTRIBUTION. Commits and reports name the friend (By: <name>) and your actual model and harness. Never claim a model or harness you are not running. A Claude worker writes the true Claude trailer.

THE TASK. nova-tools v1.2.0, stream friends-v1-2-0-reliability (general, never sprint-specific). Each harness adapter in internal/friend (adapter.go for opencode, adapter_codex.go, adapter_grok.go, adapter_antigravity.go, adapter_dsh.go, and the claude lanes of claude-oneshot-lanes) is proven only by its own unit test and a hand measurement in docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md; nothing checks the one promise they share. Write ONE end-to-end conformance check every adapter passes: deliver a message carrying a nonce on the friend's stream, the session acts on it (runs the exact `nova-friend pong` line the wake check of session-pong gives it), and a session pong with that nonce is on the bus within N minutes (a flag, default 5m). Add `nova-friend check --as <name> --harness <h> --dir <dir> [--within <d>]`: it runs the check against the live session and prints one line, `CHECK OK harness=<h> took=<d>` or `CHECK FAIL harness=<h> stage=<deliver|act|reply> why=<...>`, exit 1 on a fail. `install` runs it once after loading the agent and says the result (a fail is a NOTE, never an undone install). The unit tier runs the same check function for every harness in friend.Harnesses that has a real adapter, with a fake Exec standing in for the harness and bus.Fake for the store, so the six pass with no socket and no real time; a harness that is a Stub is reported `stage=deliver why=<its surveyed reason>`, never skipped silently. Nightly: give the exact nova-config loop record line (kind loop, on each friend's machine, running `nova-friend check` once a night) in docs/TESTING.md and in your REPORT; add no live record. Nothing that ships is a shell script: every loop or helper is a Go verb (Glenn, 2026-10-04 5:03 PM). Cite docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md from the check; one paragraph there and the verb in docs/CLI.md. Edit only the files PATHS names; a change that needs another file is a HOLD naming it. Other cards of this batch also edit docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md and docs/TESTING.md (the SHARED line): add your paragraph as its own subsection headed with this card id.

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/rowan-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of origin/rowan/integration-2026-10-04. Export GOCACHE=~/rowan-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Read AGENTS.md, docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md and docs/TESTING.md first.

STEP 2. Do the task above, writing the red test first with fakes and an injected clock; no test opens a socket or sleeps on the wall clock.
  PATHS: internal/friend/conformance*.go,cmd/nova-friend/main*.go,cmd/nova-friend/verbhelp*.go,docs/SPEC-FRIEND.md,docs/TESTING.md,docs/CLI.md
  COMMIT: delivery-conformance: one deliver, act, reply check every harness adapter passes; nova-friend check
  VERDICT: the conformance test runs for every real adapter with fakes and passes; a Stub fails at stage=deliver with its reason; nova-friend check prints CHECK OK or CHECK FAIL with the stage; install runs it once.

STEP 3. Run on a Linux bench (vision or hetzner), never on the Studio: `nice -n 10 env GOMAXPROCS=4 go test -p 2 ./internal/friend -run 'TestEveryAdapterPassesDeliveryConformance' -count=1 -timeout 600s`, then `nice -n 10 env GOMAXPROCS=4 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/friend ./cmd/nova-friend ./internal/ci`, record exact last lines, and commit only PATHS with honest attribution; `gofmt -l` on the changed files prints nothing.

STEP 4. END. Push normally with `git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/<the STATUS line's branch>`; never force. Verify `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<that branch>` equals `git rev-parse HEAD`. Write `~/rowan-working/outbox/<job>/REPORT.md` beginning `Verdict: LAND` and `Head: <full 40-hex remote tip>`, followed by one paragraph stating the change and exact gates. Use HOLD or FAIL with the precise blocker when no truthful LAND is possible. Write RESULT.md beside it carrying this card's RESULT line. Create no pull request; the sprint consumes the branch and report.

