THE TASK. Move nova-tokens onto the shared skeleton `internal/tool` and delete its private copy, same behaviour, every existing test green (moved where the lines moved, never deleted). docs/STANDARD.md (\"When building a tool\"): start from internal/tool, never from another tool's main.go; one result value rendered as lines or as JSON of the same value. Measured at the base: 2,225 non-test lines, 14 verb cases in `run` (main.go 1,491 lines), private `run`, `refuse`; internal/tool imported nowhere, verbflag in 5 files; the prose lane's head adds a private renderer `sink` (out.go, 130 lines) whose reason is \"the tool's lines are its own\" (a typed line whose token is not the verb): sk-00-tool gives the skeleton that, so `sink` goes too if your head has it. The move: one tool.Tool; the per-verb tokens (TOKENS, SOURCES, REPORT, SUM, CHECK, LEDGER, PROFILES) are each verb's `Token`; the day lines (`TOKENS DAY`, `TOKENS SOURCE`, `TOKENS AVG`) are Items of those kinds; `fold`'s 220-line body is not refactored here (that is another card): only its printing moves. The verbs' bodies stay where they are and keep their names; what goes is dispatch (the `switch`/`if verb ==` chain), the hand-written usage block, the local flag-set assembly, the private refusal printer and the private JSON writer. Every verb becomes a `tool.Verb{Name, What, Effect, Flags, Run}` whose Run returns a `*tool.Out` (Done/Fail/Refuse with Facts, Items, Notes; `Prints` for a verb that writes a payload); required flags go through `Flags.Required(name, wants)` so the refusal names every missing flag at once with its hint; `--json`, `--max`/MORE, `-h`, the exit table and the bare-command answer come from the skeleton. The printed lines may change only in the skeleton's grammar (the refusal shape, the status word, the MORE line); a change in facts, fields, exit codes or ordering is a defect. Where the skeleton cannot render a line the tool needs, say so in the PR body with the line, and keep that one verb's own printer behind a `Prints` verb, named as kept: never a second dispatcher. Update the tool's transcripts in docs/TESTS.md and its docs/CLI.md usage block to what the skeleton prints; shrink the tool's rows in internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/<tool>.txt (never raise one). Report in the PR body the lines before and after (`wc -l` of the tool's non-test .go files) as the minimal measure.

HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED (the review of wave 1 sent landed work back for each; a read applies all seven). (1) The unit of a rewrite is the sentence, not the listed line: read the whole comment or paragraph, rewrite and re-wrap the sentence, and read every changed line back as English, first word to full stop, before committing; a fragment fails the card. (2) A positive rewrite of an assertion stands only when its truth table equals the old one: the commit body writes, for each, when the old one failed and when the new one fails, the same expression; one that cannot keep its table stays and is named. (3) References are replaced only inside PATHS: a file by its full path (`git grep -n -F <dir>/<name>`), its bare name only inside its own directory; a test function by its exact name (`git grep -n -w -F`), only in its own package and the PATHS files that name it; the same name in another package is another thing and stays. (4) A measured number is a record and stays: figure, unit, past tense, and what measured it (tool version, workers, run); only names and the date go. (5) \"rule N\" of a document that still numbers its rules is a live cross-reference and stays; only a number of a list that no longer exists is history. (6) In `git diff -U0` from the start commit, a +/- line that is not a listed line or part of one's sentence (where no lines are listed: that no sentence of THE TASK asks for) fails the card. (7) A card that edits a document or data file runs in its gate the tests of every package whose _test.go reads it (`git grep -l -F <file name> -- '*_test.go'`) or that embeds it; READERS names those found when the card was cut, and the PR body names any more.

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/emma-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of the BASE branch this card names; export GOCACHE=~/emma-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Where this card says JOB.md, read BRIEF.md; where it says the staged checkout, this clone; where a step says to end as JOB.md says or with gh pr create, the END step below is the end instead: no gh, push the branch and write the outbox report.
STEP 2. Read internal/tool/tool.go and out.go (the whole API: Tool, Verb, Flags, Call, Out, Render) and one tool already on it (cmd/nova-cairn/main.go) before touching the tool.
STEP 3. Declare the verbs as tool.Verbs in main.go, point main at Tool.Main(), delete the private dispatch/usage/refusal/JSON code THE TASK names; `go build ./cmd/nova-tokens/` compiles; then run the tool's own tests and move every expected line to the skeleton's grammar (the line's facts unchanged).
