e skeleton's grammar (the refusal shape, the status word, the MORE line); a change in facts, fields, exit codes or ordering is a defect. Where the skeleton cannot render a line the tool needs, say so in the PR body with the line, and keep that one verb's own printer behind a `Prints` verb, named as kept: never a second dispatcher. Update the tool's transcripts in docs/TESTS.md and its docs/CLI.md usage block to what the skeleton prints; shrink the tool's rows in internal/ci/testdata/toolanswers/cmd/<tool>.txt (never raise one). Report in the PR body the lines before and after (`wc -l` of the tool's non-test .go files) as the minimal measure.

