     ((:id "st-release-h" :tier "-" :needs ("ot-update-release-h2")
      :title "One status grammar for nova-update release (internal/release): the standard's three words after the verb (`OK`, `REFUSED`, `FAILED`; docs/STANDARD.md section 2, AGENTS.md:71), one cap flag (`--max` with its `MORE shown=<n> total=<n>` line; "
      :brief "REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-tools
BASE: sprint/mechanical-2026-10-02
KIND: sweep
DEPENDS-ON: ot-update-release-h2
PATHS: internal/release/*.go, docs/TESTS.md, docs/CLI.md
TEST: internal/release TestAdoptWithCertifyRunsTheWorkloadsOnEachAdoptedMachineUnderTheVersionJustInstalled
READERS: ./cmd/nova-bus/ ./cmd/nova-cairn/ ./cmd/nova-check/ ./cmd/nova-ci/ ./cmd/nova-config/ ./cmd/nova-fuse/ ./cmd/nova-memory/ ./cmd/nova-redis/ ./cmd/nova-self-talk/ ./cmd/nova-sprint/ ./cmd/nova-swarm/ ./cmd/nova-table/ ./cmd/nova-tokens/ ./cmd/nova-update/ ./cmd/nova-version/ ./cmd/nova-work/ ./internal/cardhdr/ ./internal/docs/ ./internal/dogfood/ ./internal/release/ ./internal/secrets/ (tests that read or embed a file this card edits, at 48d654914aee; in the gate)
DEADLINE: finish within 180 minutes

You are a child of the coordinator: one task, one checkout, one branch, unattended. This card is the whole of the task and it stands alone in front of a stranger; nothing outside it is owed to you.
The member stages this job: you start in the job directory (export JOB=$PWD). Read $JOB/JOB.md first: it names the staged checkout (a full clone at BASE) and how this card finishes. Work in the staged checkout, commit as usual, and finish as JOB.md says. No gh, no push: JOB.md's finish does both.
Libraries considered: none needed; this card renames status words and a cap flag and adds one table-driven test with testify (already adopted). No helper is written.
The contract this card is held to is docs/STANDARD.md (embedded in AGENTS.md of the checkout): read its section 2 (a tool is for an AI), 3 (help and refusal), 4 (general, never one fleet), 5 (correct: a model where there is a machine) and 12 (class rules by name) before the first edit. Where this card and that file disagree, the file wins and the disagreement goes in the PR body.

WHAT THE EARLIER ATTEMPTS FOUND (st-release ran three or more times on flash and pro and never landed; every failure and finding, oldest first, so none repeats):
- no attempt has run yet: the card waited behind its needs; it is on the critical path (many waiting cards name it)


ATTRIBUTION: commits and reports name the friend (By: Alex) and your actual model and harness. Never claim a model or harness you are not running. A Claude worker writes the true Claude trailer.

You are a friend of the coordinator, and this card is one sprint job (docs/FRIENDS.md), delivered as `~/alex-working/inbox/<job>/BRIEF.md`: its STATUS line names the epoch, attempt and branch to push. Work only under `~/alex-working/jobs/<job>/`, using `~/alex-working/.cache/go-build`. In this card, JOB.md means the delivered BRIEF.md.


THE TASK. One status grammar for nova-update release (internal/release): the standard's three words after the verb (`OK`, `REFUSED`, `FAILED`; docs/STANDARD.md section 2, AGENTS.md:71), one cap flag (`--max` with its `MORE shown=<n> total=<n>` line; AGENTS.md:78), one refusal shape (`VERB REFUSED: <reason>; run: <remedy>`). Measured at the base: 6 `FAIL` sites: internal/release/build.go:186 (`BUILD FAIL`), cut.go:518 (`CUT FAIL`), install.go:226 (`INSTALL FAIL`), pull.go:291, :297, :302 (`PULL FAIL`); st-00-word has landed at 89fd6ecee (the skeleton's word is FAILED); ot-update-release has moved the verbs to their own binary by the time this runs, so the transcripts are under that binary's section of docs/TESTS.md and docs/CLI.md. Replace every leading `FAIL`, `NO`, `BAD` and `WARN` status word in the printed lines of PATHS with `FAILED` (a `WARN` that is advice becomes a `NOTE` continuation line; a `NO` that means the verb ran and said no is `FAILED`; a `BAD` is `FAILED` with the reason as a field), keeping every exit code exactly as it is. Every expected string in the tool's tests, its transcripts in docs/TESTS.md and its docs/CLI.md section move with the words. Add one table-driven test (`TestStatusGrammar`, in the tool's package) that runs each verb of the tool to one OK, one REFUSED and one FAILED outcome through its Run function with a fake or a fixture, and asserts the first word after the verb token and the exit code together; it opens with t.Parallel(). Change no behaviour but the words and the flag name: no verb gains or loses an exit code, no line gains or loses a field.

HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED (the review of wave 1 sent landed work back for each; a read applies all seven). (1) The unit of a rewrite is the sentence, not the listed line: read the whole comment or paragraph, rewrite and re-wrap the sentence, and read every changed line back as English, first word to full stop, before committing; a fragment fails the card. (2) A positive rewrite of an assertion stands only when its truth table equals the old one: the commit body writes, for each, when the old one failed and when the new one fails, the same expression; one that cannot keep its table stays and is named. (3) References are replaced only inside PATHS: a file by its full path (`git grep -n -F <dir>/<name>`), its bare name only inside its own directory; a test function by its exact name (`git grep -n -w -F`), only in its own package and the PATHS files that name it; the same name in another package is another thing and stays. (4) A measured number is a record and stays: figure, unit, past tense, and what measured it (tool version, workers, run); only names and the date go. (5) \"rule N\" of a document that still numbers its rules is a live cross-reference and stays; only a number of a list that no longer exists is history. (6) In `git diff -U0` from the start commit, a +/- line that is not a listed line or part of one's sentence (where no lines are listed: that no sentence of THE TASK asks for) fails the card. (7) A card that edits a document or data file runs in its gate the tests of every package whose _test.go reads it (`git grep -l -F <file name> -- '*_test.go'`) or that embeds it; READERS names those found when the card was cut, and the PR body names any more.

STEP 1. Set `JOB=~/alex-working/jobs/<job>` from BRIEF.md, create only that directory, and clone inside it: `mkdir -p \"$JOB\" && cd \"$JOB\" && git clone -q https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/nova-tools.git repo && cd repo`. Create the exact STATUS branch from the current remote tip of the BASE branch this card names; export GOCACHE=~/alex-working/.cache/go-build GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command. Where this card says JOB.md, read BRIEF.md; where it says the staged checkout, this clone; where a step says to end as JOB.md says or with gh pr create, the END step below is the end instead: no gh, push the branch and write the outbox report.
STEP 2. `grep -nE '\"[A-Z][A-Z-]+ (FAIL|NO|BAD|WARN)\\b' internal/release/*.go` lists the sites; rewrite each as THE TASK says.
STEP 3. Write TestStatusGrammar; run the tool's tests and fix every expected string the rename moved (its own `*_test.go`, docs/TESTS.md, docs/CLI.md).
STEP 4. Before committing, read `git diff -U0` against HOW THIS CARD IS JUDGED: every + line back as English to its full stop, every +/- line inside (6), no reference outside PATHS, no measured number or live \"rule N\" lost; fix and read again.
STEP 5. Run the gate, each line as written, and keep the last line of each: `gofmt -l internal/release   (prints nothing)` ; `nice -n 19 go vet ./internal/release/` ; `nice -n 19 go vet -tags functional ./internal/release/   (files under //go:build functional compile only with the tag; their tests are not run here)` ; `nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/release/ ./cmd/nova-bus/ ./cmd/nova-cairn/ ./cmd/nova-check/ ./cmd/nova-ci/ ./cmd/nova-config/ ./cmd/nova-fuse/ ./cmd/nova-memory/ ./cmd/nova-redis/ ./cmd/nova-self-talk/ ./cmd/nova-sprint/ ./cmd/nova-swarm/ ./cmd/nova-table/ ./cmd/nova-tokens/ ./cmd/nova-update/ ./cmd/nova-version/ ./cmd/nova-work/ ./internal/cardhdr/ ./internal/dogfood/ ./internal/secrets/ ./internal/docs/ ./internal/ci/`. If a test in ./internal/ci/ fails naming a ledger under internal/ci/testdata/ (\"delete the stale entry\", \"below allowed count\", \"shrink the count\"), the edit made that ledger's row stale: run `NOVA_CI_UPDATE=1 nice -n 19 go test -p 2 -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/ -run '<the failing test names, joined with |>'`, which prints `updated, rerun` and fails once; then run the gate again. Keep only the ledger lines for the files this card names: `git status --short internal/ci/testdata` and `git checkout -- <file>` for any other testdata file the update rewrote. A stale row in internal/ci/testdata/generality_text_fixtures_allowlist.txt is not rewritten by the update: delete that one row by hand. Those ledger files are the only files beyond PATHS you may change. A class test that names another ledger (tool-answers, transcripts, silent, remedy, discarded, deleted-tests) is answered the same way: its row shrinks or is deleted, never raised.
STEP 6. Commit on the checkout's own branch, message `st-release: status (*.go, TESTS.md, CLI.md)` ending with the trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude <your model> <noreply@anthropic.com>`. The pull request body states the diff stat, what was deleted (files and line counts), the gate lines with their last lines, every test added with what it pins, the three measures of docs/STANDARD.md (minimal: lines before and after; performant: any number the gate prints; correct: the model or test that holds the behaviour), and what was not done; it ends with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.
STEP 7. End as JOB.md says (docs/SPEC-CARD-CONTRACT.md): where JOB.md ends the card with its pull request (`gh pr create`), that is the end; where it asks for RESULT.md, write it in JOB.md's shape (head, branch, verdict, gate, output, report). A card whose work the base already holds at your head is `verdict: nothing` with the commit that did it; a card you could finish only in part is `verdict: partial` naming what remains, never a green claim.

RULES.
Work only in the staged checkout JOB.md names; do not clone.
Commit on the checkout's own branch, as usual; touch no other branch.
Export a private GOCACHE (the path this card names) and GOFLAGS=-mod=readonly NOVA_TEST_NO_HOST=1 before any go command.
Never `go clean`, and never clean a shared cache.
NEVER start a redis-server on this machine.
Never kill a process you did not start.
Every `go test` gets `-timeout 600s`.
No `rm -rf` outside the job directory.
Never force-push.
Never rebase.
Do not use git stash (the stash list is shared by every worktree).
Functional tests (any test that needs Redis) run ONLY inside the container through `tools/functionalrun` (`--fresh-gocache --deadline 15m`), never against any other store.
Every new test opens with `t.Parallel()`.
Run `go test -count=1 -timeout 600s ./internal/ci/` before you finish.
No names of people, machines or friends in code, comments or docs.
Docs and comments in the present tense.
Cite the model or the design section from every function that implements a rule.
Touch only the files this card names; a fix that needs another file goes into your report as a proposed diff, not a commit.
Keep the diff minimal: every added line traceable to one sentence of this card.
Commit messages end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude <your model> <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
PR bodies end with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.
Finish as JOB.md says, with `gh pr create` against the base this card names; never merge.
The PR body states the diff stat and what was deleted.
The PR body lists the tests, each with what it pins, and every local helper added.
The report is the PR: its title is the one-line report, its body every test package line and what you could not do and why.
\"Not done\" is a welcome report; a green claim you did not run is not.
A card that builds code carries a filled line `Libraries considered: <what the standard library and the adopted modules offered, and why each was used or not>` (docs/STANDARD.md section 7).
Work only in the job directory this card names.
Never force-push or rebase a shared branch.
Never start a server on this machine.
Report what was not done.

STEP 8. END. Push normally with `git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/<the STATUS line's branch>`; never force. Verify `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/<that branch>` equals `git rev-parse HEAD`. Write `~/alex-working/outbox/<job>/REPORT.md` beginning `Verdict: LAND` and `Head: <full 40-hex remote tip>`, followed by one paragraph stating the change and exact gates. Use HOLD or FAIL with the precise blocker when no truthful LAND is possible. Write RESULT.md beside it carrying this card's RESULT line. Create no pull request; the sprint consumes the branch and report.

DONE-WHEN: the TEST line's test passes at the head and the outbox report is written.")))
